hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"25051","(25051) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Locusts in al-Rabadhi were mentioned to Umar, and he said : I wish we had one or two qaf'ahs of it with us."
"25052","(25052) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abdullah, he said: I heard Abraham say: Be the mothers of the believers. They are attacked by locusts.\n(Ibn Majah 3220)"
"25053","(25053) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of his father; He used to clean locusts for Ali, and he ate them."
"25054","(25054) Abdul Rahim and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab About the locusts? He said: Omar, Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, Sahib, and Abdullah bin Omar ate it. He said: And Omar said: I wish I had a qaf’. Or two hoods."
"25055","(25055) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Wael , about Omar; He mentioned locusts and said: I wish I had a handful or two of them."
"25056","(25056) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abi Wael, on the authority of Omar; According to the hadith of Zaidah, on the authority of Al-Shaybani."
"25057","(25057) Ubayd Allah and Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Omar was eating locusts."
"25058","(25058) Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I saw Omar with his mouth watering, he said: I said: O Amir Believers, he said: I crave fried locusts."
"25059","(25059) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muthanna bin Sa’id Abi Ghaffar, who said: I heard Jabir bin Zaid saying: He would have been cut off from Locusts are more beloved to me than a piece of porridge."
"25060","(25060) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, who said: I saw my father eating locusts."
"25061","(25061) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Al-Akhdar bin Al-Ajlan, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr on the authority of locusts? He said: Eat it fried in oil."
"25062","(25062) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn al-Harith, on the authority of his father, He said: Ali was asked about locusts? He said: It is as good as sea game."
"25063","(25063) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He saw no harm in eating locusts."
"25064","(25064) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Zainab, the wife of Abi Saeed, she said: It was Abu Saeed saw us eating locusts, but he did not rebuke us, nor did he eat them. I do not know whether he was disgusted by them, or whether he He hates it?"
"25065","(25065) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hakim, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Murjanā, who said: Ibn Umar did not eat. Locusts, I said: What prevents you from eating them? He said: I disgust you."
"25066","(25066) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya; He did not eat locusts."
"25067","(25067) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not eat locusts because they would become filthy."
"25068","(25068) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman; That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about locusts? He said: Most of the soldiers of God, I do not eat it, nor forbid it. (Abu Dawud 3807, Ibn Majah 3219)"
"25069","(25069) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: The locusts were scattered by a whale."
"25070","(25070) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: It is the protrusion of a whale."
"25071","(25071) Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said about a bird that fell into a pot and died in it. He said: The broth is poured and the meat is eaten."
"25072","(25072) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: I asked him about a bird that fell into a pot and found it. It boiled, then he died? He said: The broth is spilled and the meat is eaten."
"25073","(25073) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Omar ibn Shawdhab, on the authority of Amra bint al-Tabikh, who said: My mother sent me and I bought a young boy. So I put him in a spring, and his head came out on one side and his tail on the other, so Ali, the Commander of the Faithful, passed by me and saw him, and he said: This is very good and will satisfy the family."
"25074","(25074) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mujashi’ Abi al-Rabi’, on the authority of Kuyyāl, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali was passing by. It is upon us, and it is harmful to us on our journey while we eat it. He sees no harm in it."
"25075","(25075) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about al-Jari? He said: There is nothing wrong with it, the Jews only prohibit it and we eat it."
"25076","(25076) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Amr, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no problem. In short, this is something they narrated on the authority of Ali, may God have mercy on him, in the newspapers."
"25077","(25077) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about running? He said: It is fish. If you like it, eat it."
"25078","(25078) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Mundhir al-Thawri Abi Ya`li, who said: Ibn al-Hanafiyyah was asked about running, And the spleen, and the like, which is disliked? So he recited these verses: {Say: I do not find in what was revealed to me forbidden}."
"25079","(25079) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Salma al-Sayegh, who said: I asked Ata’ bin Abi Rabah about running. He said: Every sin is fat from it."
"25080","(25080) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: On you are my sins."
"25081","(25081) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Marzuq, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Al-Hassan, who said: Al-Jari is from Sea fishing."
"25082","(25082) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in running and marmahik."
"25083","(25083) Hafs told us, he said: I heard Ja’far saying: Whatever fish does not have scales in it, we treat it and do not eat it."
"25084","(25084) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in al-Jarith."
"25085","(25085) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in eating the hareth."
"25086","(25086) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Ja’far; He brought a turtle and ate it."
"25087","(25087) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The jurists of Medina used to buy slavery. And they exaggerated it until its price reached a dinar."
"25088","(25088) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: There is no harm in eating it, meaning the turtle."
"25089","(25089) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He saw no harm in eating the turtle."
"25090","(25090) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in eating it."
"25091","(25091) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar used to order the interspersing, And he says: If it is left alone, it weakens the molars."
"25092","(25092) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’; He hated the meat and milk of Galaliya."
"25093","(25093) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the meat and milk of jalalayn."
"25094","(25094) Shababa told us, he said: Mughirah bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of His Majesty, that its flesh should be eaten, or its milk should be drunk. (Musnad 2347)"
"25095","(25095) Yahya bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: He was a donor who saw no harm in His Majesty. Hajj is performed on her, and she is eaten if most of her fodder is other than cows, and if most of her fodder is cows, then He hated her."
"25096","(25096) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He did not see any harm in eating it."
"25097","(25097) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, who said: He forbade dairy products. The majesty and its meat, and to perform Hajj and Umrah on it."
"25098","(25098) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to imprison the majestic chickens three times."
"25099","(25099) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade On the authority of the majestic milk of the sheep. (Tirmidhi 1825. Abu Dawud 3780)"
"25100","(25100) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him regarding the meat of the majestic sheep."
"25101","(25101) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Alban Al-Jalaliah."
"25102","(25102) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He had majestic camels with him, so he sent them to Al-Hama, then brought them back, and carried the camels with them to Mecca."
"25103","(25103) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Abi Zainab told us, he said: Abu Sufyan Talha told us Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best thing is vinegar. (Tirmidhi 1839 and Abu Dawud 3817)"
"25104","(25104) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best thing is vinegar. (Abu Dawud 3816. Tirmidhi 1839)"
"25105","(25105) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mu’mil, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best thing is vinegar. (Muslim 164. Ibn Majah 3316)"
"25106","(25106) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning one who is forced to die, he said: He eats what he needs."
"25107","(25107) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: If he is forced to do what is forbidden to him, then it is permissible for him."
"25108","(25108) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who was forced to eat pork and drink alcohol, he said: If he eats, he will be freed, and if he does not eat, then he will be killed. Heaven"
"25109","(25109) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Salam ibn Miskin, who said: I entered upon Jabir ibn Zayd while he was eating food. Heather grove."
"25110","(25110) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say about the servant that the magician is for the Muslim man, so she cooks for him and works for him, but he did not see that. It's unfortunate"
"25111","(25111) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Suleiman bin Misra, and Al-Mughirah bin Shubayl, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: I entered upon Salman and he had a treatment that you were taking."
"25112","(25112) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, who said: I entered upon Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz and saw Ali. Brothers, the colors of wildebeest, or he said: wildebeest of birds."
"25113","(25113) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: I saw on Anas Ibn Malik A sign of shame, and I saw a sign of shame on Al-Qasim, and I saw a sign of shame on Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah."
"25114","(25114) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Eizar bin Harith, he said: I saw Al-Hussein bin Ali He was wearing a shawl garment, and he dyed his hair with henna and katam."
"25115","(25115) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I saw on Abdullah bin Abi Awfa a place of disgrace."
"25116","(25116) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Bakra had a pricking needle. It was made of silk, and he used to wear it."
"25117","(25117) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid Abi Ziyad, who said: I saw Ali Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila He wore it until it was torn, then he tore it apart again."
"25118","(25118) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; She had a shameful garment, so she clothed it with Ibn al-Zubayr."
"25119","(25119) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I saw Al-Ahnaf bin Qays on a mule. And I saw on him a turban of disgrace, and a hat of disgrace."
"25120","(25120) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, he said: I saw Ali Qais bin Abi Hazim, And Shubail bin Awf, and Al-Sha’abi; Edges of shame, and I saw on a strip a edge of shame and a robe of shame."
"25121","(25121) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, he said: Ammar informed me, he said: I saw Abi Qaddah A face of disgrace, and I saw on Abu Hurairah a face of disgrace, and I saw countless amounts of shame on Ibn Abbas."
"25122","(25122) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, who said: I saw on Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah Prince Shame"
"25123","(25123) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: I saw on Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, and Urwah bin Al-Zubair, and upon Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, he was filled with disgrace."
"25124","(25124) Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: I saw Ali Al-Qasim and Abu Ja’far wearing robes of shame. And Abu Ja`far's garment was made of dark clay."
"25125","(25125) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Habib, who said: Ali bin Al-Hussein used to wear shameful clothes. All together"
"25126","(25126) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, who said: I sat with Sa`id bin Al-Musayyab, and I was wearing a robe of shame, so he took the sleeve of your robe and said: How beautiful this robe of yours is. He said: I said: And it is of no use to you, and it may They spoiled it for me. He said: Who spoiled it? I said: Salem. He said: If your heart is good, then wear what you like. He said: So I mentioned what Al-Hasan said, so he said: It is from the goodness of the heart. Leave the shame"
"25127","(25127) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, I asked him, I said: Were they wearing khiz? He said: They used to wear it and hate it, hoping for God’s mercy."
"25128","(25128) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I saw Muhammad bin Ali at Arafat, and he was wearing a cloak of shame. Yellow"
"25129","(25129) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Safwan bin Abdullah, who said: Saad asked permission to enter from Ibn Amir. Underneath it were robes of silk. He ordered them to be taken up, and when Saad entered, he entered wearing a robe of rags. He said to him: Have you asked permission to enter? Underneath it were saddlebags of silk. I ordered them to be taken up, and Saad said to him: What an excellent man you are, if you are not of those whom God said: {Have you lost your good things in your worldly life?} By God, for me to lie on the coals of anger is more beloved to me than to lie down On her, he said: This is on you, half of which is silk and half of it is thorns. He said: My skin is full of tingling."
"25130","(25130) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: My people told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, he said: I saw on my father"
"25131","(25131) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Khaythamiyah; Thirteen of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, were wearing shame."
"25132","(25132) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Abi Hind, who said: I saw on Abu Ubaidah a mark of disgrace, and I saw Ali Omar bin Abdul Aziz wore a white hat."
"25133","(25133) Ismail bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the hereafter. (Bukhari 5832. Muslim 21)"
"25134","(25134) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, who said: I give gifts to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He handed over a silk garment, so he gave it to Ali, and Ali put it on. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw it, he said: I hate for you what I hate for myself. Make her a source of wine among women."
"25135","(25135) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman, Ibn Numayr, and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Silk and gold are forbidden to The males of my nation are permissible for their females. (Tirmidhi 1720, Ahmad 4/392)"
"25136","(25136) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’athi, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Baraa’ said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade brocade, silk, and brocade."
"25137","(25137) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Fakhita, he said: Hubaira bin Yarim, on the authority of Ali; Verily, a garment woven with silk, either stamen or woven, was given to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he sent I brought it to me, so I came to it and said: O Messenger of God, what should I do with it? Should I wear it? He said: No, I will not accept for you what I dislike for myself, but make it wine between the fatimas. (Ibn Majah 3596)"
"25138","(25138) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Hudhayf The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from wearing silk and brocade, and said: It is for them in this world, and for you In the Hereafter\n(Muslim 1437. An-Nasa’i 9615)"
"25139","(25139) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Fakhita, he said: Ja’adah bin"
"25140","(25140) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wearing silk and gold, and said: It is for them in this world, and for us in it. The Hereafter\n(Bukhari 5831, Muslim 1637)"
"25141","(25141) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’; That Ibn Omar told him that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab saw a silk garment, and said: O Messenger of God, if you buy this What is the solution for the delegation and on Friday? He said: This is only worn by someone who has no attachment to the Hereafter. (Bukhari 8868, Muslim 1638)"
"25142","(25142) Muhammad bin Ubaid and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib. On the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Zanni, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Janni, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer. He greeted the Maghrib prayer wearing a robe, meaning a silk cloak. When he finished his prayer, he removed it violently, so I said: O Messenger God, may your blessings be upon you. He said: This is not appropriate for the righteous. (Bukhari 375. Muslim 23)"
"25143","(25143) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Omar; He used to forbid silk and brocade except that, then he pointed with his finger, then the second, then The third, then the fourth, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from it. (Bukhari 5828, Muslim 1642)"
"25144","(25144) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Kanaf, who said: I set out with Abdullah Until I came to his house, and some of his sons who had silk shirts on them came to him, so he tore them apart and said: Go to your mother, and she will clothe you. Other than this"
"25145","(25145) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fudail ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of al-Muhajir ibn Shammas, on the authority of his uncle, who said: Ibn Masoud saw His son had a silk shirt on, so he tore it apart and said: This is only for women."
"25146","(25146) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Abi al-Mughiry al-Absi, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr. He said: Hudhayf ibn al-Yaman came from a journey, and his son was clothed with silk, so he removed from it what was on his son’s males. And he left behind what he had inherited from his daughters."
"25147","(25147) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Sa`d ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf entered And with him was his son, Ali Omar, who was wearing a silk shirt. He tore the shirt open."
"25148","(25148) Ubaid bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Khalifa bin Kaab; Indeed, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr giving a sermon, he said: He said: Don’t let your women wear silk, for I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not wear silk, for whoever wears it in this world will not He will wear it in the afterlife. (Bukhari 5834, Muslim 1641)"
"25149","(25149) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abd Al-Aziz bin Abi Al-Sa’ba, on the authority of Abu Aflah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zurur Al-Ghafiqi, he heard him say: I heard Ali bin Abi Talib says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a silk garment with his left hand and gold with his right hand, then raised With whatever he gave him, he said: These are forbidden for the males of my nation, permissible for their females. (Abu Dawud 4054, Ahmad 1/115)"
"25150","(25150) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Anas bin Sirin told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Hafsah; That Atarid bin Hajib came with a brocade dress that Khosrau had covered with him, and Omar said: Shall I not buy it for you, O Messenger of God? He said: It is worn by someone who has no attachment. (Bukhari 886. Ahmad 6/288)"
"25151","(25151) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Hafs Al-Laythi, On the authority of Imran bin Husayn: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade modesty, or wearing rings with gold or silk."
"25152","(25152) Abdul Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us carrying a silk garment in one hand, and in the other. He went and said: These are forbidden to the males of my nation, permissible for their females. (Ibn Majah 3597. Tabarani 126)"
"25153","(25153) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein, on the authority of Ali bin Abdullah bin Ali, he said: My father told me that he heard Muawiyah while he was on the pulpit, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade He refrained from wearing silk and gold. (Ahmad 4/96)"
"25154","(25154) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Anas was asked about silk? He said: We seek refuge in God from its evil. We had heard that whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the hereafter."
"25155","(25155) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Tawoos; He hated wearing silk."
"25156","(25156) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated a little or a lot of silk."
"25157","(25157) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: Omar bin Abdul-Aziz wrote: Do not wear silk except what Its warp was cotton or linen."
"25158","(25158) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dressed me in a way that made me happy, and I saw anger on his face. He said: So I divided her between my wives. (Bukhari 58401 9607)"
"25159","(25159) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Dawud al-Sarraj, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: Whoever wears Silk in this world, he will not wear it in the hereafter."
"25160","(25160) Rayhan bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Marzuq bin Amr, who said: Abu Farqad said: I saw the dryings of Abu Musa. Brocade and silk."
"25161","(25161) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: My father had a piece of brocade that he used to wear during war."
"25162","(25162) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in it if it is a burden or a weapon."
"25163","(25163) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in wearing silk in war."
"25164","(25164) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders; Anas bin Malik informed them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, granted permission to Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam and to Abdul-Rahman Ibn Awf was wearing two silk shirts. He was suffering from some pain in them and they itched. (Bukhari 2919, Muslim 1646)"
"25165","(25165) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Hisham, who said: I wrote to Ibn Muhayriz. I ask him about wearing velvet and silk in places of war? He said: So he wrote: Be as strong as you are when you hate what you are forced to do when fighting, when you expose yourself to witnesses."
"25166","(25166) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ikrimah; He hated it in war, and he said: I hope for what will happen to the martyr."
"25167","(25167) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Muhammad about wearing brocade in war? He said: Where did they find the brocade?"
"25168","(25168) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, who said: We witnessed Yarmouk. He said: So Omar received us wearing brocade and silk, so he ordered us to throw stones at us. He said: So we said: What did he hear about us? He said: So we separated from him and said: He hated our adornment. When we received him, he welcomed us and said: You have come to me wearing the garb of the people of polytheism. Indeed, God did not approve of brocade for those before you, nor[corrupt] Silk"
"25169","(25169) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: I saw on Zainab bint Rasul May God bless him and grant him peace, a silk shirt from Syria. (Ibn Majah 3598. An-Nasa’i 9576)"
"25170","(25170) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit bin Zaid, he said: Hamada narrated to me, on the authority of Anisa bint Zaid; That her father entered her house wearing a silk shirt, and he came out angry."
"25171","(25171) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, on the authority of Omar; He said: It is not suitable for him except like this. One finger, or two fingers, or three fingers, or four fingers."
"25172","(25172) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Omar said: Do not wear Silk except two or three fingers."
"25173","(25173) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He did not see any harm in the flags."
"25174","(25174) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Umar, the client of Asma’, who said: I saw Ibn Umar buying A turban with a flag, so he called for the two camels and cut them. I mentioned that to her, and she said: Misery for the servant of God, O neighbour. She came on the robe of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she came with an embroidered robe with the sleeves, the pocket, and the two vultures. With brocade.\n(Muslim 1441, Abu Dawud 4051)"
"25175","(25175) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a cloak. It was worn by a woman wearing a silk brocade."
"25176","(25176) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to hate to wear a garment in vain. Silk, or its woven fabric, and they see no harm in flags."
"25177","(25177) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to wear a tanned palanquin."
"25178","(25178) Abdullah bin Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: My father had a volcano in which there were flags of four fingers. Preamble"
"25179","(25179) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah, who said: I saw on Al-Aswad bin Hilal a tanned palanquin. Long"
"25180","(25180) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, who said: I saw a turban on Abdullah ibn Yazid. Rolled, rolled."
"25181","(25181) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ismail bin Imran al-Abdi, he said: I saw Ali Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, a tanned tongue."
"25182","(25182) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I saw Ali Al-Qasim wearing a turban with a white silk border."
"25183","(25183) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abd al-Malik, who said: I saw on Abu Ja`far a long, marked robe."
"25184","(25184) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, the client of Hudhayfy, who said: I saw on Abd Allah ibn Ma`qil a tongue. It has brocade buttons."
"25185","(25185) Ibn Fudayl and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Burra, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: Avoid what He mixed the silk of the clothes."
"25186","(25186) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Dawud Al-Hafari narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin He neglected to say, on the authority of Omar, that he said: Silk is not suitable unless it is tied or buttoned."
"25187","(25187) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Muslim al-Bateen, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani said: A sheikh came and greeted Ali, and he was wearing a long robe with a brocade in front of it. Ali said: What? Is this stink under your beard? So the Sheikh looked right and left and said: I don’t see anything. He said: The man says: He only meant the brocade. He said: The man says: Then we will meet him and will not return."
"25188","(25188) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murā, on the authority of Hudhayfă; He saw a man wearing a frill and brocade buttons, and he said: He is imitating the chains of Satan."
"25189","(25189) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They both disliked knowledge on clothing."
"25190","(25190) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid; That Ibn Omar bought a turban and saw a flag on it, so he cut it."
"25191","(25191) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Abdullah; That Qais bin Abbad came to Muawiyah and dressed him in a garment, then parted her flag and put it on."
"25192","(25192) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaid, on the authority of Khalid bin Yasar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: We used to cut off Flags"
"25193","(25193) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawa bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to cover his daughters and his wives with silk wine."
"25194","(25194) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Salem: The man covers his family with silk and wine. And the clothes, and he said: I may not have clothed them with them, so they continued to have them until I clothed them with them, and if you did not clothe them with them, So, by God, it is better."
"25195","(25195) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They both hated silk and ibrahim."
"25196","(25196) Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Atiyya, he said: I saw Ibn Umar taking a saber-like angel, or a slave, and gathered them together. With his hand, then he threw it away."
"25197","(25197) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; He hated wearing thin saree clothes."
"25198","(25198) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid, who said: I saw Ali Al-Qasim wearing a long robe with a flag on it."
"25199","(25199) Abu Bakr told us, he said: Ibn Aliyah said, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Anis Abi Al-Aryan, he said: I saw Ali Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ali wore a thin shirt and a thin turban."
"25200","(25200) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Habib, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas wearing a silk shirt. Delicate, his garment was cleaned of its delicacy."
"25201","(25201) Al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: Abu Israel narrated to us, saying: The judge used to cover his turban with a saber turban."
"25202","(25202) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Malik, who said: I saw on Abu Ja`far a long, marked robe."
"25203","(25203) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated thin clothes."
"25204","(25204) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: I saw Al-Qasim wearing a thin robe."
"25205","(25205) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Silk is more beloved to me than saber."
"25206","(25206) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Khayyat, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He had a delicate robe."
"25207","(25207) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I have never seen someone more beautiful than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted someone wearing a red robe. (Bukhari 3551. Muslim 92)"
"25208","(25208) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I saw Nafi’ bin Jubayr With the lameness, and upon it is saffron."
"25209","(25209) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of the common people, he said: I saw on Ibrahim al-Taymi and Ibrahim al-Nakha’i Each one of them is wearing a red veil."
"25210","(25210) Ubaidullah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Amr bin Othman, on the authority of Musa bin Talha. That Talha was wearing saffron."
"25211","(25211) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Othman, who said: I saw a red veil on Abu Ja’far."
"25212","(25212) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Karim, who said: I saw Ibrahim wearing a yellow garment."
"25213","(25213) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: He saw no harm in a man wearing dyed clothing. With safflower or saffron."
"25214","(25214) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: I saw a red veil on Ash-Sha’bi."
"25215","(25215) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Asim ibn Badla, who said: I encountered people who were taking This night they are dressed in saffron, some of them are: Zar, and Abu Wael."
"25216","(25216) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nasr bin Aws, who said: I saw Ali bin Al-Hussein wearing a red veil."
"25217","(25217) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: We, the family of Muhammad, wear saffron."
"25218","(25218) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The musaffar was the dress of the Arabs, and I do not know anything about it. He destroyed it in Islam, but he did not see any harm in it."
"25219","(25219) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that he used to dye a garment for him for a dinar. So he wears it."
"25220","(25220) Ishaq ibn Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Salma ibn Bakht, who said: I saw on Abu Ja`far al-Mu’safarat, or Al-Musafar, and I saw on him a deterrent from creation."
"25221","(25221) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Ibrahim wearing a red veil. Satisfied"
"25222","(25222) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Waqid narrated to me, saying: Abdullah bin Buraydah narrated to me, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving us a sermon, and Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein came wearing shirts. Red\n(Abu Dawud 1102. Tirmidhi 3774)"
"25223","(25223) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim On the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw me. He greeted me while I was wearing a taffy garment and said: Throw it on, for it is the garment of the infidels. (Muslim 27 Ahmad 2/207)"
"25224","(25224) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hunayn, who said: I heard Ali saying: He forbade me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I do not say that I forbid you, about wearing saffron. (Muslim 1449. Abu Dawud 4041)"
"25225","(25225) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, on the authority of Ibn Hunayn, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: Do not wear a red, ruddy garment."
"25226","(25226) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: We came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Adhakhir, and he turned to me, wearing a garment covered with safflower. He said: What is this? So I knew what he hated, so I came to my family while they were covering their ovens, so I threw it in him, then I came to him the next day, and he said : Oh Abdullah, what did you do with the band? So I told him, and he said: Don’t let some of your family clothe you, for there is no problem with that for women."
"25227","(25227) Ali told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Suhail, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: No. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Al-Qasiyyah and Al-Fuddum. Yazeed said: I said to Al-Hasan: What is Al-Fuddum? He said: The one saturated with safflower. (Bazzar 476)"
"25228","(25228) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Tamim Al-Khuza’i, he said: An old woman of ours narrated to us, she said: I was seeing When Omar saw a man wearing a dyed garment, he struck him and said: Leave these bright garments for the women."
"25229","(25229) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Nafi’; Ibn Umar saw his son’s hair dyed, so he forbade him."
"25230","(25230) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; Indeed, they disliked tampering and anything above it for men."
"25231","(25231) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He hated the saffron for men."
"25232","(25232) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Mawhib, he said: My uncle narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Uthman, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of saffron."
"25233","(25233) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to enter with Alqamah while the lions were on the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he would see them in the red quilts. He said: And Abraham did not see any harm in cutting the safflower."
"25234","(25234) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. Indeed, they did not see any harm in women’s red hair."
"25235","(25235) Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikiya, who said: I saw Umm Salamah wearing armor and a veil. You are full of safflower."
"25236","(25236) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim; Aisha was wearing yellow clothes, and she was a mahram."
"25237","(25237) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim; Aisha used to wear clothes dyed with safflower, and she was a mahram."
"25238","(25238) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Tamim Al-Khuza’i, he said: An old woman told us, she said: Omar said: Leave These sparkles are for women."
"25239","(25239) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima bint al-Mundhir; Asmaa was wearing musaffar while she was in ihram."
"25240","(25240) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He saw some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulating the Kaaba, wearing saffron clothes."
"25241","(25241) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He did not see any harm in women’s hair dyeing."
"25242","(25242) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of his sister Sakina, she said: I entered with my mother. On Aisha, and I saw on her a red shield and a black veil."
"25243","(25243) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Malik; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to dye his clothes with saffron, even his turbans. (Abu Dawud 4061. Ahmad 2/126)"
"25244","(25244) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Omar ibn Jawan, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, who said: Uthman came with Ali A yellow mantle, with which he covered his head. (Hakim 361)"
"25245","(25245) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun; Omar was wearing a yellow garment the day he was injured."
"25246","(25246) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: I saw Ali wearing a yellow shirt and loincloth."
"25247","(25247) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of a man from the descendants of Az-Zubay, called: Abbad ibn Hamza. Al-Zubair ibn Al-Awwam was wearing a yellow turban while he was wearing it, so the angels descended with yellow turbans on him."
"25248","(25248) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I saw Ibn al-Hanafiyyah wearing a yellow cloak."
"25249","(25249) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I saw Musab bin Saad wearing a garment. Yellow, and he is sitting with the poor."
"25250","(25250) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: I saw Ali wearing a yellow garment. And Khamisah."
"25251","(25251) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Amr bin Marzuq, who said: I saw Ibrahim wearing a yellow garment."
"25252","(25252) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hanash bin Al-Harith, he said: I saw Ibrahim wearing a yellow robe, and a yellow garment."
"25253","(25253) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Mughul, on the authority of Ukil, who said: I never saw Ibrahim in the summer. Except that he was wearing a yellow quilt and a yellow garment."
"25254","(25254) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, he said: I saw Hammad praying with a yellow garment on him."
"25255","(25255) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: I saw Abdullah bin Al-Hassan wearing a yellow quilt, and he was hiding in it. The Grand Mosque."
"25256","(25256) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Shurahbil, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us and we put water for him to cool off with, so he washed, then I came to him. With a yellow quilt, and I saw traces of rust on his ankles. (Abu Dawud 5143. Ahmad 3/421)"
"25257","(25257) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yasar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He was asked about furs? He said: I love her so much."
"25258","(25258) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I saw on Ibrahim some fur dung."
"25259","(25259) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Kibran, he said: I saw on al-Dahhak some fur droppings."
"25260","(25260) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Ibn Umar saw a man. He was pleased with its softness and said: If I knew this was intelligent, I would be pleased to have a garment from it."
"25261","(25261) Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Thabit, who said: I was sitting with Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Layla, a man with two huge dreadlocks came to him and said to him: O Abu Issa. He said to him: Yes. He said to him: Tell me what you heard about Al-Farra’. He said: I heard my father saying: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man came to him. He said: O Messenger of God, should I pray in furs? He said: Where is the tanner? (Ahmad 4/348)"
"25262","(25262) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad, and Nafi’. Aisha ordered one of her family members to put off his fur when he prayed."
"25263","(25263) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibn Jabr, who said: I saw Ali Sa’id bin Jubayr drawing fur dung, and he said: I only wore it to be seen on me, or to be asked about it."
"25264","(25264) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; He said regarding furs from the skins of the dead: I wish I had some of it and could wear it."
"25265","(25265) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Muti’, he said: Abu Husayn narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I went out with Abu Wael until we came to the furriers. He bought a fur, and the owner of the fur said: I will give you more, Abu Wael. He was smart and said: I am not happy that I bought what you said for a Qirat. Abu Husayn said: Ibrahim used to say that, and Saeed bin Jubayr used to say that."
"25266","(25266) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Wa Ali, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whatever skin is tanned will be purified. (Muslim 278 and Abu Dawud 4120)"
"25267","(25267) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Salman, he said: It was for some The mothers of the believers lost their lives, and she died, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by her and said: It would not harm her family if they benefited. With her grace (Ibn Majah 3611)"
"25268","(25268) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maymunah; A sheep of your master, Maimounah, passed by by her and she had given her some of the sadaqah while dead, and he said: No, they will take away my return. So they tanned it and benefited from it? They said: O Messenger of God, is she dead? He said: It is forbidden to eat it. (Muslim 2761, Abu Dawud 4117)"
"25269","(25269) Hushaym told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Ikrimah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; A sheep of Sawda bint Zam’a died. She said: So we tanned its skin, and we used to reject it until it became grey. (Bukhari 6686)"
"25270","(25270) Hushaym told us, saying: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a sheep belonging to Sawda bint Zam’a, and he said: Do they not benefit from her gift? He tanned and purified himself."
"25271","(25271) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ismail, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: A tanner who cleaned her hair."
"25272","(25272) Khaled told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Yazid ibn Qusayt, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his mother, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that the skins of the dead be enjoyed.\n(Abu Dawud 4121, Ibn Majah 3612)"
"25273","(25273) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by a sheep of a master of Maymun in Mitti, and he said: May they benefit from my generosity. (Muslim 104. Ahmad 1/277)"
"25274","(25274) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maimunah, she said: One of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Have you not benefited? With her grace\n(Muslim 1031, Ahmad 1/277)"
"25275","(25275) Hushaym told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: I told that the Messenger of God prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He passed by a dead sheep and said: It would not harm its people if they benefited from its generosity."
"25276","(25276) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqa, on the authority of his grandfather, Riyah ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: Tanning"
"25277","(25277) Abu Khaled narrated to us, not by Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his commander, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of John ibn Qatada, on the authority of Salamah bin Muhabaq said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He tanned hides.\n(Ahmad 3/476. Daraqutni 12)"
"25278","(25278) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of John bin Qatadah, on the authority of Salma bin Muhabiq, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example. (Abu Dawud 4122. Ahmad 5/6)"
"25279","(25279) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of John bin Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Likewise, Mansour did not mention Salama bin Muhabqq."
"25280","(25280) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: The tanner of the dead person cleans it."
"25281","(25281) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that he was asked about Silk and gold for women? He said: They are your toys, so decorate them with whatever you wish."
"25282","(25282) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I make it easier for women to have sexual intercourse. Silk and gold, then he recited: (Is he who is brought up in adornments while he is in a dispute not clear?)"
"25283","(25283) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ali; Indeed, Akkadir Doumah gave the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a silk garment, so he gave it to Ali, and he said: He divided it with wine. Among the women\n(Muslim 18. Abu Dawud 4040)"
"25284","(25284) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said regarding silk and gold: Forbidden for the males of my nation, permissible for their females."
"25285","(25285) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Muammar, who told him, on the authority of Az-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: I saw Ali Zainab The daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a silk shirt, Sira."
"25286","(25286) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ma’qil bin Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, he said: There is no harm in silk. Brocade is for women, but it is disliked for them if it describes or is transparent."
"25287","(25287) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: I clothe my daughters with silk. And the most beautiful of them is gold."
"25288","(25288) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Yazid Al-Muzani, he said: Omar was the Prophet Al-Nasa’ about wearing the Qabat, and they said: It does not dry, so he said: If it does not dry, then it is dry."
"25289","(25289) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, that Omar said: Do not let your women wear Qabatiya, for it is only He will heal and describe."
"25290","(25290) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to dislike women wearing the Qabat clothing, and he said: It only makes it dry and clear."
"25291","(25291) Hatem bin Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: One day, one of the Copts of Egypt, one of the Copts of Egypt, clothed Ibn Umar. So Ibn Umar sent and summoned him and said: What do you want to do? He said: I want to make it a shield for my two companions. Ibn Omar said: If it is not dry, then it will dry."
"25292","(25292) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Daqra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We do not wear clothes. In which is the cross."
"25293","(25293) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahhaf[corrupt] He said: I asked Abu Jafar about a coffin in which I have statues? He said: Tell me about someone who saw Omar burning a garment with a cross on it, then removing the cross from it."
"25294","(25294) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw on some of his wives a veil with a cross on it, so he ordered it to be removed."
"25295","(25295) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thabit bin Adiy, who said: I did not see Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas visiting them. Their shirt was cut off."
"25296","(25296) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Al-Aizar, on the authority of Saeed Al-Madani, he said: I was with Abu Hurairah was at his funeral, and I saw him with a yellow beard and his buttons unbuttoned."
"25297","(25297) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Urwah bin Abdullah bin Qushayr, he said: He narrated to me. Muawiyah bin Quran, on the authority of his father, said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I pledged allegiance to him, even though his shirt was Mutlaq, Urwah said: I did not see Muawiyah, nor his son, in the winter, nor any free man, except with their garments loosened. (Tirmidhi 58, Abu Dawud 4079)"
"25298","(25298) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, who said: I did not see Saeed bin Al-Musayyab cheering for him. Izarah Qat."
"25299","(25299) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama, he said: I have never seen Salim visit him."
"25300","(25300) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, who said: I saw Salim with his garments loose."
"25301","(25301) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us, on the authority of his father; He saw Ali Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya wearing a garment with his buttons unbuttoned, and he had a robe of shame."
"25302","(25302) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Maimun, who said: I did not see Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab unbuttoned."
"25303","(25303) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman and Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of his uncle Abdul Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade pulling the garment. (Abu Ali 5129. Ahmed 320)"
"25304","(25304) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Jabaliya, and Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever drags his garment out of his imagination, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.\n(Bukhari 5791, Muslim 1652)"
"25305","(25305) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said : Indeed, he who drags his garment is arrogant, and God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. (Muslim 1651. Ahmad 2/55)"
"25306","(25306) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever drags his garment out of vanity, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: I met Ibn Umar. In the court, he said: So I mentioned to him the hadith of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he pointed to his ears: My ears heard it, and my heart understood it. (Ibn Majah 3570)"
"25307","(25307) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He passed by my father. He saw a young man from Quraysh as he was dragging his way, and he said: O son of my brother, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: Whoever drags his garment out of vanity, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. (Ibn Majah 3571. Ahmad 2/503)"
"25308","(25308) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, he said: Sa’id ibn narrated to us Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God does not look to a path. (Ahmad 1/322, Tabarani 12413)"
"25309","(25309) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd The Most Gracious, that he heard Abdullah bin Omar say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God does not look at the one who dares. His robes are virtuous.\n(Ahmad 2/69)"
"25310","(25310) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali ibn Mudarrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Kharsha ibn al-Hurr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are three to whom God will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look. To them, and He will not purify them, and for them is a painful punishment. He who gives way, who is generous, and who spends is spoiled by false oaths. (Muslim 1020, Abu Dawud 4084)"
"25311","(25311) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was said: Whoever touches his garment like his ankle will not May his prayers be accepted. He said: And Dharr said: Whoever touches his garment to the ground, his prayers will not be accepted."
"25312","(25312) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: A young man entered On Omar, so the young man began to praise him. He said: Then Omar saw him pulling his garment, so he said to him: O son of my brother, raise your garment. Indeed, he is the most pious to your Lord and the purest for your garment. He said: Then Abdullah used to say: How strange it is for Omar to see the rights of God upon him. Nothing in him prevented him from speaking about it."
"25313","(25313) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Ibn Masoud; He was untying his garment, and something was said to him, and he said: I am a man with shaky legs."
"25314","(25314) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Dhail, he said: Abu Bakr asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, about the place of the garment? He said: It has a tapered shank. There is no good in what is below that, and there is no good in what is above that."
"25315","(25315) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim bin Nazir, on the authority of Hudhayf, who said: The Messenger of God took May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with the lower leg muscle, or shin, and he said: This is the place of the garment. If you refuse, then lower. If you refuse, then lower it. If you refuse, then the lower garment has no right to the lower garment. (Tirmidhi 1783 and Ibn Majah 3572)"
"25316","(25316) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: I heard Abu Nabiyyah saying: I heard Aisha saying : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is under the ankle of the garment will be in Hell. (Ahmad 6/59)"
"25317","(25317) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ya’four, he said: I saw Ibn Umar and his lower garment extended to half of his legs, or Close to half of his legs."
"25318","(25318) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Abdul Rahman bin Yaqoub, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The believer’s garment extends to half the shin, but it was not To the Ka'b there is no harm, and whatever is below the Ka'b is in the Fire. (Abu Dawud 4090. Ahmad 3/30)"
"25319","(25319) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Ghaffar, on the authority of Abu Tamimah Al-Hajmi, on the authority of Abu Jari Al-Hujaimi, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. He said: Do not say: Peace be upon you? For, peace be upon you, you revive the dead. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, increase me. He said: The lower garment to half the shin, if you refuse. Then to the Ka'ab, and beware of imagination, for God does not like imagination. (Abu Dawud 4081. Tirmidhi 2721)"
"25320","(25320) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far, who said: Maymun used to roll up his garment to the middle of his shins."
"25321","(25321) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahib narrated to us, he said: Dawud bin Abi Hind narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Qaza’i, on the authority of Al-Asqa’ Ibn Al-Asla', on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: What is lower than the ankles of the garment in Fire (Ahmed 5/9)"
"25322","(25322) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Umayya; That Ali girded himself, so his garment clung to his knees."
"25323","(25323) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The place of the garment is at the point of the shank."
"25324","(25324) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The lower garment reaches half the shin, or to the ankles, no. Better than what is lower than that."
"25325","(25325) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They used to hate the garment above half of the shin."
"25326","(25326) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Suleiman bin Mushir, on the authority of Kharshah; That Omar called for a blade and lifted a man’s lower garment from his ankles, then cut off what was below that, and said: It is as if I were seeing To his fly running down his heel."
"25327","(25327) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw some of the Companions of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon them. They girdle themselves with half of their market. He mentioned Usama bin Zayd, Ibn Umar, and Zayd bin Arqam. And Al-Bara’ bin Aazib."
"25328","(25328) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas He puts on his garment and spreads his garment from between his hands, until the two hems of it fall on the backs of his feet, and he raises them from delayed\n(Abu Dawud 4093. An-Nasa’i 9681)"
"25329","(25329) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Sulayman al-Mukhtab narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Ali wearing a garment. Najrani up to the middle of his legs."
"25330","(25330) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Diqan, who said: I saw Abu Sa`id and Ibn Umar being treated in half. Their market"
"25331","(25331) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Iyas ibn Salama, on the authority of his father; Othman bin Affan had his lower garment extending to half of his shins. He said: So he was told about that? He said: This is the garment of my beloved, meaning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Tirmidhi 121, Bazzar 353)"
"25332","(25332) Yazeed bin Harun told us, saying: Sharik informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Husayn bin Qabisa, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Sufyan bin Sahl, no. Let him go, for God does not like those who let go. (Ahmad 4/246. Ibn Hibban 5442)"
"25333","(25333) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Asir ibn Jabir: He used to hate slippers and sandals. Which was not mentioned."
"25334","(25334) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; Aisha used to hate furs that were not slaughtered."
"25335","(25335) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He was among those who disliked praying without prayer. He will be remembered; Omar, Ibn Omar, Imran bin Husayn, Aisha, and Asir bin Jabir."
"25336","(25336) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, who said: The shirts of Omar bin Abd were Al-Aziz and his clothes between the ankle and the shrine."
"25337","(25337) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawad, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: The shedding of the garment, the shirt, and the turban. Whoever wears any of them is arrogant, God will not look at him. On the Day of Resurrection\n(Abu Dawud 4091, Ibn Majah 3576)"
"25338","(25338) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Sulayman al-Ahwal, on the authority of Mujahid He said: The shirt and the loincloth are the same."
"25339","(25339) Yazeed told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Yasar, he said: They mentioned with Ikrimah Jarr The shirt and the loincloth, and he said: By God, it is worse and worse."
"25340","(25340) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: His shirt was above the garment. And the robe is over the shirt."
"25341","(25341) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, who said: I saw Al-Qasim’s shirt reaching to the ankle."
"25342","(25342) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awanana, on the authority of Mughirah, who said: Abraham’s shirt was on the back of The foot"
"25343","(25343) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Umair, who said: I saw Salem’s shirt rolled up above the ankles, and he said: I I saw Ibn Omar whose shirt was like this."
"25344","(25344) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of Ali, who said: Ali bought a Sunblanese shirt for four Dirhams, and he called the tailor, and he extended the sleeves of the shirt, and ordered him to cut off what was behind his fingers."
"25345","(25345) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Saeed Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi. ; Omar bin Al-Khattab called for a blade to cut the sleeve of the shirt of Utba bin Farqad from his fingertips, and he was on it. A Sunbulani shirt, and he said: I am sufficient for you, O Commander of the Faithful. I am ashamed of you cutting it off in front of the people. So he left him."
"25346","(25346) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, he said: I saw Ali on him. A mid-calf, or raziqi shirt. When he extends it, it reaches half of his legs, and when he extends it, it does not exceed his nails."
"25347","(25347) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Buhturi, who said: I saw Anas bin Malik with the sleeves of his shirt down to the wrist."
"25348","(25348) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa the Teacher, on the authority of Badil al-Uqaili, who said: The sleeve of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And peace be upon him.\n(Abu Dawud 4023. Tirmidhi 1765)"
"25349","(25349) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, he said: Abu Al-Ala told me, he said: I saw Ali is girded above the navel."
"25350","(25350) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qadamah ibn Musa, on the authority of his father, who said: I prayed beside Ibn Umar, and he had girded himself. Above the navel, so he pulled it until he placed it lower than it."
"25351","(25351) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; Indeed, they were covering themselves below the navel."
"25352","(25352) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, who said: I saw Ali bin Al-Hussein’s white hood. Distracted"
"25353","(25353) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I saw on Ibn al-Zubayr a hood that had a shelf. He takes shade with it when he circumambulates the Kaaba."
"25354","(25354) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, who said: I saw on Abraham’s hood surrounded by foxes. Or a beaver."
"25355","(25355) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, he said: I saw on Al-Dahhak the hood of foxes."
"25356","(25356) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his father; That Abu Musa came out of the toilet, wearing a hood, so he wiped over it."
"25357","(25357) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Mughīrī, on the authority of Ali ibn Rabi’, he said: I saw Ali Yetzer, and I saw straw on him."
"25358","(25358) Abdă narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Whenever Aisha went out as a pilgrim, or She was a pilgrim, and she took out her servants with her to move around her, and they used to feel their feet up to the mule’s belly. So she commanded them to wear cloaks."
"25359","(25359) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: Salman said: What an excellent garment is the turban."
"25360","(25360) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Habib, who said: A vision was seen on Ammar bin Yasir Tabban while he was in Arafat."
"25361","(25361) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, who said: My father used to wear turban under the garment."
"25362","(25362) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I saw Abu Sadiq girding his garment, and I saw under his garment there was straw."
"25363","(25363) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, who said: I saw Ali ibn Rabi’a al-Walbi showing a sign. He said: The sheikh, meaning Ali, used to wear it."
"25364","(25364) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; She used to order her servants to wear cloaks while they were in ihram."
"25365","(25365) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: It was Abu Musa. When he sleeps, he wears fibre, for fear that his private parts will be exposed."
"25366","(25366) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: They cut off Ride, and get out on the horses, and put on your sandals, and put on sandals, and put on your trousers, and put on your girdles, and throw away your belongings. And you should wear contagious clothing, and beware of the guidance of non-Arabs, for the worst of guidance is the guidance of non-Arabs."
"25367","(25367) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Qays, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. May God bless him and grant him peace, so he bargained with us for trousers."
"25368","(25368) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muadh bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: Ali addressed us with the Kufa. And he has trousers on."
"25369","(25369) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hafs bin Abi Mansour, who said: I saw trousers on Al-Sha’abi."
"25370","(25370) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi, who said: When it was winter, Al-Hasan would wear ink trousers and hats. Ink"
"25371","(25371) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Omar’s letter came: “Throw away your trousers and put on garments.”"
"25372","(25372) Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Wasil, the client of Abu Uyaynah, who said: Indeed, God Almighty revealed to Abraham: You are the most honorable of creation to me, so when you pray, the earth will not see your private parts, and wear trousers."
"25373","(25373) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, he said: I saw Abu Al-Aaliyah wearing trousers, he said: So I said: Why? He said: It is men's clothing."
"25374","(25374) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammam informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father On the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Eat and drink and give in charity, and wear clothing that is not mixed with extravagance. And no imagination. (Ibn Majah 3605. Ahmad 2/181)"
"25375","(25375) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Eat whatever you want. And wear whatever you want, as long as two traits do not make you wrong: extravagance or imagination."
"25376","(25376) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the Almighty’s saying: {And those who, when they spend, are neither extravagant nor stingy, and have sustenance in between.} He said: Do not starve them. And do not expose yourself to them, and do not spend anything that people will say: You have been extravagant in it."
"25377","(25377) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Uthman al-Haatibi, who said: Tell me who saw Uthman wearing a garment. Strongly"
"25378","(25378) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: Ali bin Abi Talib came out He is wearing a cotton shirt and two tartan scarves."
"25379","(25379) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Ata’ Abi Muhammad, who said: I saw Ali wearing a shirt of this type. Carabies without washing."
"25380","(25380) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Maymoon Abul-Qasim, who said: I saw Ata’ wearing an oily shirt."
"25381","(25381) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled Abi Al-Ala’, who said: I saw Al-Hasan wearing a dirty shirt."
"25382","(25382) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I saw a thick shirt on him."
"25383","(25383) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib Al-Taifi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Sa’ib bin Abi Hindi, on the authority of his father, He said: I saw two Qatari dresses on Omar."
"25384","(25384) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mutayr ibn Tha’labiya, on the authority of Abu An-Nawar, who said: I saw Ali buying two shirts. Two thick ones are better than the one of them."
"25385","(25385) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’i, who said: I saw Ali wearing two garments. Qataris."
"25386","(25386) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There were those before you who wore thinner clothes. And He has compassion for hearts."
"25387","(25387) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Talha, who said: Talha bin Ubaid, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out. Two embroidered dresses."
"25388","(25388) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Saar, on the authority of Umm Salamah She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: How much does a woman drag by her tail? He said: A hand span. She said: Then we will reveal it? He said: An cubit, do not exceed it. (Abu Dawud 4115. Ahmad 2/55)"
"25389","(25389) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave them a span of a span in the tail, so come to Us and we will arm them. With a reed an cubit.\n(Abu Dawud 4116. Ahmad 2/18)"
"25390","(25390) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave Fatima a hand span, then said: This is the value of your tail."
"25391","(25391) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. ; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Fatima, or Umm Salamah: This is an cubit. (Ibn Majah 3583. Ahmad 2/263)"
"25392","(25392) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Khaled, he said: The woman was commanded to make her tail an arm's length."
"25393","(25393) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They saw no harm in fleecing the dead. And lint hair."
"25394","(25394) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Khaliq, on the authority of Hammad in the wool of the dead: If he is washed, His remembrances"
"25395","(25395) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad; They did not see any harm in using the wool of the dead to benefit from it, and Al-Hasan said: It should be washed."
"25396","(25396) Yazid told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: They did not see with wool or hair, And Al-Mar'azi, and Al-Wabar are mighty, but they disliked praying in the skin."
"25397","(25397) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the feathers, the heel, the wool, and the bones of the dead. He said: If he is washed, then he is pure."
"25398","(25398) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; The daughters of Hussein bin Ali used to wear shirts, so when they reached puberty and married, they would wear armor."
"25399","(25399) Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hammad, who said: There is no harm in the feathers of the dead."
"25400","(25400) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Abu Rafi’, he said: I saw Abu Bakr and he had a fine garment that he would leave on when he rode, and I would wear it for him. And when We came down, and this is the garment for which you lent a weight, they said: This is the garment we sold after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"25401","(25401) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, he said: Abu Hajj Moses is on a red camel, his head is covered, and he has a cloak on him."
"25402","(25402) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It was for the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. A garment called Al-Marut is not wide, by God, nor soft."
"25403","(25403) Abu Asama told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burda. He said: I went to see Aisha and she brought out to me a thick garment made in Yemen, and a garment made of this type. Which you call Al-Mullabidah, so she swore: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would die in it. (Bukhari 3108, Muslim 35)"
"25404","(25404) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of his father, he said: So he said to me: My son, if you had witnessed us while we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the heavens struck us, you would have thought that our scent was a scent. The lamb (Abu Dawud 4030. Tirmidhi 2479)"
"25405","(25405) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kharash, he said: I saw Abu Dharr and he was He sits on a piece of sackcloth and shawls."
"25406","(25406) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Abbad Al-Mazini, on the authority of Abi Majlaz, who said: The companions of Ibn Masoud pinched the hail, He said: Then the man became ashamed to come wearing short clothes, or short clothes. He said, so Abu Abd al-Rahman began wearing his abaya. Then he became there in the morning, then he rose there on the third day, and the people began to retreat."
"25407","(25407) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin al-Ghaz narrated to us, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, on the authority of Salman; He had a love of Abaa, and he was the prince of the people."
"25408","(25408) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: It was Jesus. Bin Maryam wears hair."
"25409","(25409) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Mughiriya, who said: Abraham did not see any harm in wearing clothes. A man's garment is worth fifty dirhams, meaning the garment."
"25410","(25410) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, he said: It was not He exaggerates with a garment, unless it is with a tongue."
"25411","(25411) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Tamim had a robe that he bought for a thousand. He prays in it."
"25412","(25412) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Waqid, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Umar used to clothe a man among the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is worth nine hundred percent."
"25413","(25413) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, who said: It was stolen and should not be exaggerated. With a garment, except with a tongue."
"25414","(25414) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, who said: He was wearing stolen clothes. Linen under cotton."
"25415","(25415) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qur’a ibn Khalid, who said: I said to Ibn Sirin: What was Abu Hurairah’s clothing? He said: Like these two garments, and over him are two torn linen garments. So he blew his nose and said: Blow, squirt, Abu is blowing his nose. A kitten in linen."
"25416","(25416) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If one of you puts on shoes, he should start with the right, and if he takes them off, he should start with the left. (Muslim 1660. Ahmad 2/233)"
"25417","(25417) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When he put on his shoes, he started with the right, and when he took them off, he started with the left."
"25418","(25418) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; It was recommended that when he put it on, he should start with the right hand, and when he took it off, he should start with the left."
"25419","(25419) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: If you wear clothes, then start With the right, and if you remove it, start with the left."
"25420","(25420) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of a cousin of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Ubaid bin Umair was He starts by taking off the left hand, then he takes off the right and puts it on the left."
"25421","(25421) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: None of you should walk in just one sandal, nor in one pair of slippers. To take them both off, or to walk on them both. (Bukhari 58550 Muslim 1660)"
"25422","(25422) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: He came out to us He struck his forehead with his hand, then said: You are telling a lie about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I bear witness to the fact that I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: If one of you’s limbs are cut off, he should not walk in the other until He fixes it.\n(Bukhari 9561 Muslim 69)"
"25423","(25423) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; Concerning the one who walks in a single shoe, he said: They hate it, and they say: No, not even a single step."
"25424","(25424) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Taman, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Do not walk in sandals. The one"
"25425","(25425) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: If one of you’s limbs are cut off, He should not walk in single shoes."
"25426","(25426) Abu Dawud Al-Hafari told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr cut off. So he took off his sandal and fixed it."
"25427","(25427) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of a man from Muzainah, who said: I saw Ali He would walk in a single shoe in the cities, and he would make up his shoes."
"25428","(25428) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not see any harm in walking in a single shoe if its joints were cut off, and there was nothing between it and it being repaired. How great is it?"
"25429","(25429) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father; Aisha used to walk in a single slipper, and she said: I would make Abu Hurairah angry."
"25430","(25430) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Zaid bin Muhammad; He saw Salem bin Abdullah walking in a single sandal."
"25431","(25431) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: It was mentioned in the presence of Muhammad that a man should wear shoes while standing, and he said: I do not know of any harm in it."
"25432","(25432) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uqba, he said: I saw Abraham putting his feet into his sandals. And He is standing."
"25433","(25433) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, who said: I saw Yahya bin Wathhab wearing shoes standing."
"25434","(25434) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: I saw Al-Hasan wearing shoes standing."
"25435","(25435) It has informed me on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: We have been informed that Ali was shod and standing."
"25436","(25436) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He disliked for a man to wear shoes while standing. (Ibn Majah 3618)"
"25437","(25437) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; The sandals of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had two sides, and the sandals of Abu Bakr and Umar. (Tirmidhi 86. Bazzar 2961)"
"25438","(25438) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: It was for the sandals of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Majah 3615. Ahmad 3/122)"
"25439","(25439) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw Ibn Umar’s shoes wearing a qabbalan."
"25440","(25440) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: The example of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was to wear two waists. You are following me. (Ibn Saad 478)"
"25441","(25441) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, who said: They were the sandals of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. It has two partners, two qabalan and two partners. (Tirmidhi 76. Ibn Saad 478)"
"25442","(25442) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, he said: I saw the sandal of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in Medina, covered, smooth, and with an outside back. (Ibn Saad 478)"
"25443","(25443) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan; He heard Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair saying: Rayhani told me; That her family sent her and with her a boy wearing bells, and he said: Tell your family that this man is following you. Satan"
"25444","(25444) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I came to Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla and I had a piece of wheat, so he said: Do you want to wear a copy of the Qur’an with it? I said: No, he said: Do you wear a sword with it? He said: I said: Make it beautiful for my daughter. He said: Could you please make it bells? It is disliked."
"25445","(25445) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hanash, who said: I saw Ibn Umar and a boy was brought to him. He made light of it, and he made it easy for you."
"25446","(25446) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A boy was brought to Aisha with a jingle, and she said: Why do I see you repulsing the angels? Take her away from me."
"25447","(25447) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I was informed that Muhammad used to cut off the rattles that were on the Boys"
"25448","(25448) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Abraham adorned two of his young daughters with golden jingles. They vote for us."
"25449","(25449) Our companions told us, on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, who said: I entered upon Omar ibn Abdul Aziz and saw He has two daughters, both of whom wear cloaks."
"25450","(25450) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musawar, on the authority of Ja`far bin Amr bin Harith, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon while wearing a black turban. (Ahmad 4/307, Ibn Saad 455)"
"25451","(25451) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Al-Ansari, he said: I saw Ali wore a black turban on the day Uthman was killed."
"25452","(25452) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca wearing a black turban. (Tirmidhi 1735. Abu Dawud 4073)"
"25453","(25453) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Al-Anbas Amr bin Marwan told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Ali A black turban, with two ends hanging at the back."
"25454","(25454) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abul-Fadl, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It was the turban of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"25455","(25455) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salma bin Wardan, who said: I saw Anas wearing a black turban without a hood. He relaxed it behind him."
"25456","(25456) Waki’ told us, he said: Asim bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr wearing a turban. Black, he swayed her behind him, about an arm's length away."
"25457","(25457) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Abi Hind narrated to us, saying: I saw Abi Ubaidah wearing a black turban."
"25458","(25458) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Milhan ibn Tharwan, who said: I saw Ammar wearing a turban. Black"
"25459","(25459) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Dinar Abu Omar narrated to us, saying: I saw a black turban on Al-Hasan."
"25460","(25460) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: Tell me who saw Ali having become black. With a black turban, which he loosened between his hands and behind him."
"25461","(25461) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah, he said: I saw Ali Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid has black headbands."
"25462","(25462) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Gabriel’s turban was On the day Pharaoh drowned, black."
"25463","(25463) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ayman, who said: I saw a turban on Ibn al-Hanafiyah. Black"
"25464","(25464) Al-Bakrawi told us, on the authority of Abu Issa, on the authority of Abu Ziyad, who said: A sheikh came, who is called: Salem. He said: : I saw Abi Darda’ wearing a black turban."
"25465","(25465) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said: I saw a black turban on the black man."
"25466","(25466) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Musa bin Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca on the day of the conquest wearing a black scarf. (Ibn Majah 3586)"
"25467","(25467) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, he said: Hazal Al-Khathami narrated to us, he said: I saw Ali Al-Baraa’ A black turban."
"25468","(25468) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mukhariq, on the authority of Ata, who said: I saw on Abdul Rahman Ibn Awf, wearing a black turban."
"25469","(25469) Ma’an told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Yunus, who said: I saw Ali and his turbans were black."
"25470","(25470) Shadhan narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ali addressed us on the day Friday, wearing a black turban."
"25471","(25471) Shababi told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, who said: I saw Abu Nadhr with a black turban on him."
"25472","(25472) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Al-Sha’bi wearing a white turban. He has relaxed both sides of it and has not sent it."
"25473","(25473) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abdul-Malik narrated to us, saying: I saw Sa`id bin Jubayr wearing a turban. White"
"25474","(25474) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I saw Al-Ahnaf standing on his mule, and I saw Shame on his turban."
"25475","(25475) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Salam bin Shaddad Abi Talut, who said: I saw disgrace on Anas bin Malik’s turban."
"25476","(25476) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun."
"25477","(25477) Abu Usama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar informed us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar used to use Uttam, And he placed it between his shoulders.\n Ubaidullah said: Our sheikhs told us that they saw the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, darkening and relaxing it. Between their shoulders."
"25478","(25478) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr wearing a veil. He had loosened the ends of the turban between His hands"
"25479","(25479) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas Amr bin Marwan, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Ali, may God be pleased with him He has a turban with two ends loosened."
"25480","(25480) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salama bin Wardan, who said: I saw Anas wearing a turban that he had left behind him."
"25481","(25481) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Musawar, he said: Ja’far bin Amr bin Harith narrated to me, on the authority of his father, he said: As if I look at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing a black turban, the ends of which he has relaxed between his shoulders.\n(Muslim 453. Abu Dawud 4074)"
"25482","(25482) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, who said: I saw Ibn Umar wearing a blindfold who had loosened his turbans from between him. His front and behind him, and I do not know which of them is longer."
"25483","(25483) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhul, who said: I saw him turning dark and not letting the edge of his turban loose."
"25484","(25484) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: I saw on a piece of turban that he had left behind him."
"25485","(25485) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Salim and Al-Qasim; They used to hang their turbans between their shoulders."
"25486","(25486) Shababih told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, who said: I saw Abu Nadhru wearing a black turban. He released her from under his neck."
"25487","(25487) Shababā told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I saw Al-Hasan wearing a black turban with two ends hanging down behind him."
"25488","(25488) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, who said: I saw a sharīḥ covering a single kurah."
"25489","(25489) Sulayman bin Harb narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Hakim, on the authority of Sulayman bin Abu Abdullah said: I realized that the first immigrants wore turbans like black, white, red, and green ones. And zero, one of them puts the turban on his head, and puts the hood on top of it, then turns the turban around like this, He means on his hair, he does not take it out from under his chin."
"25490","(25490) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, who said: I saw Zayd bin Thabit wearing a garment and a robe. And his turban."
"25491","(25491) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid; He hated to be dark unless he put a turban under his beard and ring."
"25492","(25492) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr; I saw Ali Abdullah bin Al-Zubair wearing a suit."
"25493","(25493) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: I saw on Ibn al-Zubayr a hood with a shelf. It means Bartala."
"25494","(25494) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issa bin Taman, who said: I saw a banner on Anas bin Malik."
"25495","(25495) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: I saw a robe on Shurayh."
"25496","(25496) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Shihab, he said: I saw a banner on Sa’id bin Jubayr."
"25497","(25497) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr (h) and on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Wear foxes, and do not pray in them."
"25498","(25498) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sudair, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: It was Ali bin Hussein’s. Spongona foxes."
"25499","(25499) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, he said: I saw on Al-Dahhak the hood of foxes."
"25500","(25500) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, who said: I saw on Abraham a hood surrounded by foxes, or Beaver"
"25501","(25501) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He heard Abu Salama and Suleiman bin Yassar tell about Abu Hurairah, informing the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: The Jews and Christians do not dye, so differ from them. (Muslim 80. Ibn Majah 3621)"
"25502","(25502) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Abu Quhafiya was brought on the day of The conquest went to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as if his head were clogged, and he said: Take him to some of his wives. So let them change it, and spare it the blackness.\n(Muslim 1463 and Abu Dawud 4201)"
"25503","(25503) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Du’ali, on the authority of Abu Dhar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best thing you have changed with gray hair is henna and concealment.\n(Tirmidhi 1753. Ahmad 5/150)"
"25504","(25504) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Talha narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Wahhab, on the authority of Tawus, or Ibn Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: A man who had dyed his hair with henna passed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: How beautiful this is, then Another man who had dyed his hair with henna and katam passed by and said: This is better than that. He said: Then another man who had dyed his hair with yellow passed by. He said: This is better than all of these. He said: And a peacock was whistling.\n(Abu Dawud 4208, Ibn Saad 440)"
"25505","(25505) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Ansari, he said: I saw Abu Bakr, his head and beard were as if they were burning coals of anger."
"25506","(25506) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The best of what you have changed. Gray hair, henna and muteness."
"25507","(25507) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I saw Ibn al-Hanafiyya and his head and beard were Two bottles that he dyed with henna and katam."
"25508","(25508) Abu Asamah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I saw Abdullah bin Abi pay his respects to Zafran. Dyed with henna."
"25509","(25509) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: I saw a man getting his hair dyed with henna."
"25510","(25510) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, who said: I said to Abu Jafar: Did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, dye his hair? He said: He touched some henna and katam."
"25511","(25511) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Salam bin Abi Muti’ narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Mawhib, he said: I entered upon Umm He greeted him, and she brought out to me some of the hair of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dyed with henna and katam.\n(Ibn Majah 2423. Ibn Saad 437)"
"25512","(25512) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Nabel, who said: I saw a peacock dyeing his hair with henna."
"25513","(25513) Ibn Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mughiriya ibn Shubayl, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: It was Abu Bakr comes out to us, as if his beard was matted with henna and concealment."
"25514","(25514) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Maqlid, on the authority of Amir, who said: Ali only became bitter in his colour."
"25515","(25515) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: I saw Anas bin Malik and Abdullah bin Abi Fuller and their hair is red."
"25516","(25516) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Eizar bin Harith, he said: Al-Hussein bin Ali was It is dyed with henna and katam."
"25517","(25517) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, he said: I saw with the family of Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah Ibn Zam'a dyed some of the hair of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Saad 437)"
"25518","(25518) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf said that Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad bin Abd Yaghouth was a companion of theirs and he was white. The head and the beard, so he went to them one day and had redd them, and the people said to him: This is better, so he said: My mother is Aisha. Yesterday she sent her two maids to me and she swore to me that she would dye me, and she told me that Abu Bakr used to dye me."
"25519","(25519) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Hassan told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I saw Thamud, and I saw his hair dyed. Weld them"
"25520","(25520) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Qais, a servant of Khabbab, who said: I entered On Al-Hassan and Al-Hussein while they were dyed black."
"25521","(25521) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman, who said: I saw Musa bin Talhayi dyeing his hair with the sign."
"25522","(25522) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muwaib, who said: I saw Nafi’ bin Jubayr getting his hair dyed. In black"
"25523","(25523) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he saw no harm in dyeing black."
"25524","(25524) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: They were asking Muhammad about dyeing black, and he said: I do not know. Very bad"
"25525","(25525) Waki’ and Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama, that it was It is dyed black."
"25526","(25526) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in using the mark. With vegetables"
"25527","(25527) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, who said: I asked Ibn al-Hanafiyyah about pigment. With the mark, he said: These are our servants, Ahl al-Bayt."
"25528","(25528) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: Abu Ja`far used to dye his hair with two-thirds of henna and one-third of its name."
"25529","(25529) Shababi told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, he said: Abu Ashana Al-Maafiri told us, he said: I saw his buttocks. Ibn Amir dyed his hair black and said: We blacken its tops but its roots refuse. (Ibn Saad 343)"
"25530","(25530) Al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Ayyub, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib narrated to me that Abu Al-Khair He narrated to him, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that he used to dye his hair with a tree that is said to be: the dye is the blackest black. (Bukhari 1661, Muslim 25)"
"25531","(25531) Ibn Yaman narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: He used to dye his hair With the name"
"25532","(25532) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, he said: Ata’ was asked about dyeing with markings, and he said: It is one of the Speaking of people, I saw a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I did not see any of them dyeing their hair. With the name, they did not dye their hair except with henna, katam, and this yellow."
"25533","(25533) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Rabah, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked dyeing black and said: The first one to dye his hair with it was Pharaoh."
"25534","(25534) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Mujahid, that he hated dyeing In black"
"25535","(25535) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, that he disliked dyeing with dye and said: Abu Bakr dyed With henna and concealment."
"25536","(25536) Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Muslim, who said: Al-Sha’bi was asked about dyeing pigment with birthmarks, his idea."
"25537","(25537) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Musa bin Najdah, on the authority of his grandfather Zayd bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I asked Abu Huraira: What do you think about pigmentation with the mark? He said: The one who uses his hair dye will not smell the scent of Paradise."
"25538","(25538) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr. He was asked about dyeing with paint, what he thought of it, and he said: God covers the servant with light in his face, then extinguishes it. In black"
"25539","(25539) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, about Ata’ in the field of dyeing with markers, and he said: It is modern."
"25540","(25540) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Saad, who said: I saw Uthman bin Affan was building Al-Zawra’ on a white mule with a yellowish beard."
"25541","(25541) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Al-Aizar, on the authority of Saeed Al-Madani, he said: I was with Abu Hurairah was at his funeral and was dyeing his beard."
"25542","(25542) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hilal, he said: Sawadah bin Hanzala told me, he said: I saw Ali with a yellow beard."
"25543","(25543) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I saw Zayd ibn Wahhab dyeing his beard."
"25544","(25544) Ghandar Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar. They whistle for their beards."
"25545","(25545) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to dye his beard."
"25546","(25546) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: I saw Abu Umamiya whistling."
"25547","(25547) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, who said: I saw Abdullah bin Busr yellowing his beard and head."
"25548","(25548) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Zaid, Salama’s client, who said: I saw Salama yellowing his beard."
"25549","(25549) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: I saw a Qais whistling his beard, and I saw Shubail ibn Awf had his beard yellow, and he was one of the people of Taylasiyah."
"25550","(25550) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled bin Dinar, who said: I saw Anas, Abu al-Aaliyah, and Abu al-Sawwar whistling. Weld them"
"25551","(25551) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, he said: I saw Abu Wael, Al-Qasim, and Ata turning their meat yellow."
"25552","(25552) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Dawud Abi Al-Yaman, who said: I saw Abdullah bin Abi Awfa whistling. Her beard"
"25553","(25553) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id; Ibn Juraij asked Ibn Omar, saying: I saw you dyeing your beard with rust? Ibn Omar said: As for the yellowing of my beard, I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, yellowing his beard."
"25554","(25554) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, who said: I saw Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’abi combing his hair. With yellow, and I saw Jarir bin Abdullah dyeing his hair with yellow and saffron."
"25555","(25555) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I saw the lions and Ibn Al-Aswad whistling their beards."
"25556","(25556) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of al-Mustamir ibn al-Rayyan, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza’i; He used to dye his beard, and Abu Nadhra used to dye his beard."
"25557","(25557) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Issa bin Taman, who said: I saw a man dyeing his beard."
"25558","(25558) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Ghasil, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, he said: Jabir bin came to us Abdullah, his eyesight has been damaged, and his beard and head have turned yellow with rust."
"25559","(25559) Al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: Ibn Al-Ghaseel narrated to us, saying: I saw Sahl bin Saad with a yellow beard. Jammaima."
"25560","(25560) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, who said: I saw Jabir bin Samurah dyeing his beard."
"25561","(25561) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Utai Al-Tamimi, he said: I saw my father White head and beard."
"25562","(25562) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: I saw Ali with a white head and beard. It filled what was between his shoulders."
"25563","(25563) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, he said: Abu Amir Salih bin Rustum told us, he said: Humaid bin Hilal told us, he said: Al-Ahnaf bin Qais told me, he said: I came to Medina and entered its mosque, and while I was praying a tall man entered. His beard was white and his head was shaved, resembling parts of it. So I went out and followed him. I said: Who is this? They said: Abu Dharr."
"25564","(25564) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Mustamil, he said: I saw Jabir bin Zaid with a white beard."
"25565","(25565) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, who said: I saw a mujahid with very white hair and beard, and I saw Saeed bin Jabir, white-bearded."
"25566","(25566) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw Ali bald, with white hair and beard."
"25567","(25567) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Sudair bin Al-Sayrifi, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw Ali with a white head. And the beard"
"25568","(25568) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Sulaiman Abi Mawdud, who said: I saw al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid has white hair and beard."
"25569","(25569) Shababi told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Othman, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr with a white beard. And I saw a white-bearded peacock."
"25570","(25570) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hariz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr Al-Salami, who said: We came to him while we were young men. We did not know what to ask him about, so I said to him, or some of us said to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a young man. Or an old man? He said: There were white hairs on her neck. (Bukhari 3546. Ahmed 187)"
"25571","(25571) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Juhayfa, he said: I saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Muslim 1822, Ibn Majah 3628)"
"25572","(25572) Al-Muttalib bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, he said: I saw Al-Hussein bin Ali and his corpse was emerging from beneath me. His turban"
"25573","(25573) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Umm Hani’ said: The Prophet entered, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he has four glands, which means braids. (Tirmidhi 1781 and Abu Dawud 4188)"
"25574","(25574) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: I saw Ibn Umar and Jabir, and each one of them had a collection of things."
"25575","(25575) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, who said: Abdullah had hair. He puts it on his ears."
"25576","(25576) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Aflah narrated to us, saying: I saw Al-Qasim’s entire collection."
"25577","(25577) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ubaid bin Umair had two characteristics."
"25578","(25578) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, joked He, peace and blessings be upon him, greeted Abu Qatada. He said: I will shear your sheep. He said: You have her place as a prisoner. Then he said to him after that: Honor her. After that, he used to take her as a slave. (Tabarani 675)"
"25579","(25579) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Zaid, on the authority of his father; That there was a wolf in the head of Al-Hasan bin Ali, and that Al-Hussein bin Ali forced him with it until he bleed, or He made you sore."
"25580","(25580) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Mu’aqib, he said: He was a scholar of jurisprudence. He said: Someone from my family who I do not blame told me that he saw a man with his forelock placed between his eyes, and he saw Saad bin Malik like that"
"25581","(25581) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The People of the Book used to let their hair down, and the polytheists used to part their heads, and it was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, loves to agree with the People of the Book in what was not commanded. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, then he parted after that. (Bukhari 3558. Muslim 91)"
"25582","(25582) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I used to stand behind the mouth of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then lower the Her forelock.\n(Abu Dawud 4186. Ibn Majah 3633)"
"25583","(25583) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, he said: There was poetry The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, felt a man’s hair between his ears and his shoulders. (Bukhari 5905. Muslim 1819)"
"25584","(25584) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I have not seen someone more beautiful than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted, walking, wearing a red suit."
"25585","(25585) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, he said: Iyad bin Laqit narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Rimtha, he said: I came and saw a man sitting in the shade of the Kaaba, and my father said: Do you know who this is? This is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When we came to him, behold, there was a man with plenty of wealth and a shield. Two green dresses. (Ahmad 4/163)"
"25586","(25586) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ayman, who said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr with a camel up to the neck, and he was It makes a difference"
"25587","(25587) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, who said: I saw Ubaid ibn Umair, and Ibn al-Hanafiyy for each One of them all."
"25588","(25588) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Habib, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas with a large group of people."
"25589","(25589) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, on the authority of Rashid ibn Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded Peace be upon him, peace be upon him, and he forbade silence."
"25590","(25590) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, who said: We were sitting with Ali, and he called Ibn To him, it was said to him: Othman, then a boy with a tail came to him."
"25591","(25591) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Radhi bin Abi Aqeel, on the authority of his father, who said: We were at the door of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, Then a son with a wolf came out."
"25592","(25592) Malik narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Ghaziyya narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, Zuhayr said: He sees Amara, on the authority of his father. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The beautiful poetry, or The beautiful is the one whom God has clothed and honored. He said: And he hated removing it. Zuhayr claimed that it was humiliation."
"25593","(25593) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I saw Ibn Omar’s camel separated, hitting its shoulders."
"25594","(25594) Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Kamil, on the authority of Habib, who said: It is as if I am looking at Ibn Abbas, and he has a great collection of talents."
"25595","(25595) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother Isa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abu Layla said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you wears a new garment, let him say: Praise be to God. He who has clothed me with what I conceal my private parts with, and with which I beautify myself in front of people."
"25596","(25596) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Asbagh bin Zaid told us, he said: Abu Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Abu In front of him, he said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab put on a new garment, and he said: Praise be to God who has clothed me with my private parts, and I can beautify myself. In my lifetime, then, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whoever wears a new garment, and says: Praise To God, who has clothed me with what I concealed my private parts with, and made my life more beautiful with it. Then he went to the garment with which He was created, or he said: He threw it and gave it in charity. It was in God’s protection, in God’s protection, and under God’s protection, alive and dead. He said it three times.\n(Tirmidhi 3560, Hakim 193)"
"25597","(25597) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of a man from Muzainah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw Omar wearing a washed garment, and he said: Should you new this garment of yours? He said: Washing, O Messenger of God. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Wear new clothes, and live praising, and he died. A witness, may God give you comfort in this world and the hereafter. (Ibn Saad 329, Musnad 986)"
"25598","(25598) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abi Wahhab, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, who said: If he wears The man saw the new garment, and said: O God, make it a blessed garment in which we may be grateful for Your blessings, and in which we may improve Your worship. And we act therein in obedience to You. It does not go beyond his collarbone until he is forgiven."
"25599","(25599) Ibn Aliya narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nazra, who said: They were the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And when they see someone wearing a new garment, they say: You will wear it out, and may God reward you."
"25600","(25600) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, who said: We only live in the back."
"25601","(25601) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Aoun bin Abdullah narrated to us, he said: A man wore a garment. Then he praised God and was admitted to Paradise, or forgiven. He said: Then a man said: I will not return to my family until I have put on a garment. New, and thank God for it."
"25602","(25602) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Asama, he said: When it was a Friday, Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to He sent guards and they took the doors of the mosque, but they did not find a man with any hair left behind except to cut him off."
"25603","(25603) Muawiyah bin Hisham and Sufyan bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father On the authority of Wael bin Hajar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw me with long hair, and he said: Flies, flies, so I set off. So I took it, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw me and said: I did not help you, and this is better.\n(Abu Dawud 4187. Ibn Majah 3636)"
"25604","(25604) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Qadamah, who said: A man entered upon Ibn Sirin, and he was wearing hair. It was long, so he said: This is something he disliked. Then he came in on it the next day and had removed it, so he said: This is something he disliked."
"25605","(25605) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took He handed over a paper seal, then engraved on it; Muhammad is the Messenger of God, then he said: No one should engrave the inscription of my seal on this one.\n(Bukhari 5866 and Muslim 55)"
"25606","(25606) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fabricated He handed over a ring to him, and said: We have made a ring and engraved an inscription on it, so no one should inscribe it on it.\n(Bukhari 5874 Muslim 2092)"
"25607","(25607) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Hudhaifa, She said: There were two pillars facing each other at the end of it, and it was written: Praise be to God."
"25608","(25608) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, and Al-Hasan, who said: The inscription on the seal of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was: Muhammad. Messenger of God"
"25609","(25609) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The inscription on Anas’s ring was of a crouching lion with prey around him."
"25610","(25610) Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad; The inscription on Al-Ash'ari's seal was of a lion between two legs."
"25611","(25611) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Ata told us, on the authority of his father, he said: He was the seal of Imran. Ibn Husayn engraved a statue of a man wearing a sword. Abraham said: I saw it in a clay ring with us, and my father said: This is the ring of Imran bin Husayn."
"25612","(25612) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: In the seal of Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah were the five wounds of Allah."
"25613","(25613) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was in the seal of Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah. Praise be to God."
"25614","(25614) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The seal of Abdullah bin Omar was Abdullah bin Omar."
"25615","(25615) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was in the seal of Abu Ubaidah bin The surgeon, praise be to God."
"25616","(25616) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was the engraving of the seal of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon Muhammad, the Messenger of God."
"25617","(25617) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, who said: There was an engraving of a stolen ring. In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."
"25618","(25618) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: The engraving of Abraham’s ring was, O God, and there were flies in it."
"25619","(25619) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: It was in the seal of Abi Al-Izza, for God’s sake, all of them."
"25620","(25620) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The engraving of the ring of Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad was gradual."
"25621","(25621) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: The inscription of Muhammad’s ring was his nickname."
"25622","(25622) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: His ring was engraved with lines. Ibn Abu Adi: I found it written."
"25623","(25623) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, he said: I saw Ali Al-Qasim and Salim two seals, with Al-Qasim’s seal his name, and in Seal of Salem, whose name is"
"25624","(25624) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; He did not see any harm in a man writing “Allah suffices me” in his end, and the like."
"25625","(25625) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Abu Awan narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; Omar said: Do not inscribe or write in Arabic on your rings."
"25626","(25626) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: It was in the seal of Ali, may God bless him and grant him peace. The king"
"25627","(25627) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He was the seal of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Muhammad is the Messenger of God."
"25628","(25628) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Indeed, he disliked writing all the verses in the seal, and he did not see any harm in mentioning God with the seal."
"25629","(25629) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, that he disliked having the verses inscribed in his ring. Complete"
"25630","(25630) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: There was mention of Allah in the seal of Hasan and Hussein. Jafar said: And it was in the seal of Abu Al-Izza that belongs to all of him."
"25631","(25631) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Sidqi bin Yasar, who said: I said to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: What Should I write in my end? He said: Write in it the remembrance of God, and say: He commanded me to do so happily."
"25632","(25632) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, who said: There was an engraving of a stolen ring. In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."
"25633","(25633) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say: No. It is harmful for all verses to be engraved in the seal."
"25634","(25634) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He disliked the verses being inscribed in the ring."
"25635","(25635) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, a seal made of paper."
"25636","(25636) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Tawus, who said: It was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He held a silver ring in his hand, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: You have a look, and this is a look you have given him. This day, he took it away and gave it to a man. (Ibn Saad 470)"
"25637","(25637) Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Az-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: It was on the seal of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May peace and blessings be upon him, and his family was an Ethiopian. (Bukhari 5868 and Muslim 62)"
"25638","(25638) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, took He handed him a paper ring, and it was in his hand, then it was in the hand of Abu Bakr after him, then it was in the hand of Omar, then It was in the hands of Othman until he fell into the Arees Well, and its inscription was Muhammad, the Messenger of God. (Bukhari 5873. Ahmad 2/22)"
"25639","(25639) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Tell me who saw an iron ring on Abdullah."
"25640","(25640) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I saw an iron ring on Ibrahim."
"25641","(25641) Zaid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Rashid told us, he said: Makhul told us, he said: He was the seal of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, smooth iron, with silver on it, clear. (Ibn Saad 473)"
"25642","(25642) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Muhammad was asked about the iron ring? He said: There is no problem, unless his scent is unpleasant."
"25643","(25443) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I saw on Abraham an iron ring. He said: So I told him, he said: It was Abdullah's iron ring."
"25644","(25444) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir; Omar saw an iron ring on a man and he thought of it."
"25645","(25445) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hakim Ibn Al-Daylam, who said: I heard Al-Dahhak, he said: Ata was asked about A silver ring with an iron ring? His thoughts"
"25646","(25446) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Saad, on the authority of Abu Al-Kanood, he said: He was afflicted. One of the great ones on the Day of Muharran. So I put a ring on him and put it on. Ibn Masoud saw it on me, so he took it and put it on. between two of his molars and broke them, then threw them to me, then said: Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us About the gold ring. (Tayalisi 3861, Ahmad 1/377)"
"25647","(25647) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Suhail, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, about the gold ring. (Ahmed 99)"
"25648","(25448) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’athi, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Baraa’ said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us from using our seals with gold."
"25649","(25449) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of His father, Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, who said: The Negus was brought to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. His jewelry contained a gold ring and an Ethiopian stone, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took it. He said hello with a stick, but he turned away from it, or with some of his fingers, and he turned away from it. Then he called his son and his daughter before you. The daughter of Abi Al-Aas, so he said: Be beautiful with this, my sons. (Abu Dawud 4232. Ahmad 6/119)"
"25650","(25650) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was in I have a gold ring on my finger, so Omar ibn al-Khattab gave it to me, and I saw that he was just looking at it, so I relaxed my hand. So he took it and took it away, but I did not ask him about it nor did I ask for it."
"25651","(25651) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seal things with a seal. From gold, he came out to the people and they started looking at him, so he put his right hand on his little finger, then he returned to The house was thrown away."
"25652","(25652) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein, he said: My mother told me, on the authority of my father, He said: I entered upon Umm Salamah when I was a boy and I was wearing a gold ring, and she said: O my maid, give her to me. So she gave her to me. She said: Take it to his family and make a seal of paper. I said: My family has no need for it. She said: So give him alms, and make a paper ring for him."
"25653","(25653) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: He saw Abdullah in the hand of Khabbab A gold ring, and he said: Isn’t it time for this to be put away yet? He said: Yes, you will not see it on me after that."
"25654","(25654) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Awf ibn Malik, who said: I came to Omar and on my hand was a ring from He went and hit my hand with a stick that she had with him."
"25655","(25655) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: Sa`id bin Jubayr saw a gold ring on a young man from the Ansar. He said to him: Do you not have a sister? He said: Yes, he said: So give it to him."
"25656","(25656) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated the gold ring."
"25657","(25657) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Uqba bin Wasaj, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about gold? He said: We used to hate it for men."
"25658","(25658) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas; He hated the gold ring."
"25659","(25659) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Omar saw a gold ring on the hand of a man. He forbade it."
"25660","(25660) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw on Al-Baraa’ a gold ring."
"25661","(25661) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Hudhayfa, She said: He had a gold ring on his hand that contained a ruby."
"25662","(25662) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad; He was wearing a gold ring."
"25663","(25663) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ismail, he said: It was narrated to me by someone who He saw Talha bin Ubaid Allah and Saad, and mentioned six or seven of them with gold rings."
"25664","(25664) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymimi, who said: They used to make concessions for the boy to have a ring. Gold. When he grows up, he throws it out, or he says: he throws it out."
"25665","(25665) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Simak, he said: I saw a ring on Jabir bin Samra. Of gold, and I saw a gold ring on Ikrimah."
"25666","(25666) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Mughul, on the authority of Abul-Safar, who said: I saw a gold ring on Al-Bara’."
"25667","(25667) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, who said: I saw Ali Abdullah bin Yazid has a gold ring."
"25668","(25668) Ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, he said: Hamza bin Abi Asid narrated to us, and Al-Zubayr narrated to us. Ibn Al-Mundhir Ibn Abi Asid, they said: We took a gold ring from Abi Asid’s hand when he died, and he was a Badr."
"25669","(25669) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Qasim Al-Azdi, who said: I asked Anas bin Malik: Should I be sealed with a ring? He went? He said: Yes, and if you wish of silver, it will not harm you, but do not feed from any vessel of gold or silver."
"25670","(25670) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to make his portion from what was left of his hand."
"25671","(25671) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to make his palm from what was on the inside of his palm."
"25672","(25672) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, who said: When Ikrimah entered the toilet, he would make his mouth from what was next to his stomach. Enough"
"25673","(25673) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein used to be sealed. Yesarama (Tirmidhi 1743)"
"25674","(25674) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; That Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman were sealed on their left sides."
"25675","(25675) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ubaidullah, he said: I saw Al-Qasim and Salim encircling their rings."
"25676","(25676) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: I saw a seal on Abraham’s left wrist."
"25677","(25677) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to wear a ring in his left hand."
"25678","(25678) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I saw Abraham’s ring on his left hand."
"25679","(25679) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Salt, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman used to have their left fingers sealed."
"25680","(25680) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail Al-Azraq, who said: I saw the ring of Amr bin Harith on his wrist."
"25681","(25681) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Ja’far bin Abdullah bin Ja’far; Jafar bin Abi Talib was sealed in his oath. (Ibn Saad 36)"
"25682","(25682) Ma’an told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Saad, who said: I saw Muhammad bin Ali making the seal in his right hand."
"25683","(25683) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Abdullah bin Nawfal, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas And his seal is in his right hand, and I only think that he mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was like that. He wears it\n(Tirmidhi 1742 and Abu Dawud 4226)"
"25684","(25684) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make a seal in his right hand. (Ibn Majah 3647; Abu Ali 6794)"
"25685","(25685) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Abi Rafi’, the client of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed me. May God bless him and grant him peace; That Abdullah bin Jaafar used to seal the seal in his right hand, and he claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seal the In his right hand (Tirmidhi 1744. Ahmad 1/205)"
"25686","(25686) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Dalham bin Salih Al-Kindi narrated to us, on the authority of Hujair bin Abdullah Al-Kindi, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father; Al-Najashi presented two simple black slippers to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he wore them."
"25687","(25687) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sawadah bin Abi Al-Aswad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: You must wear these black slippers, so wear them, for it is more appropriate for you to wipe over them."
"25688","(25688) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Urwah bin Abdullah bin Qushayr, who said: I heard Abu Ja’far saying: The sword of Omar was the one who was standing. Silver, so I said: Commander of the Faithful? He said: Commander of the Faithful."
"25689","(25689) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi al-Hasan, he said: Its cap was the sword of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made of silver. (Tirmidhi 1691 and Abu Dawud 2577)"
"25690","(25690) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: Al-Zubayr’s sword was decorated with silver."
"25691","(25691) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Hakim narrated to us, saying: I saw a nail on the stand of Sahl bin Hanif’s sword. He went"
"25692","(25692) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Mughul told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Omar’s sword was a pointed sword, so I said to him: Omar. Hello? He said: I saw Ibn Omar imitating him."
"25693","(25693) Wakī’ narrated to us, Abu Al-Umays narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Abdullah’s sword was drawn."
"25694","(25694) Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, on the authority of Qur’a ibn Khalid, on the authority of Abu Wahshiyya al-Siqal, who said: Mus’ab called me and came out to me. Two swords, and he said: Which of these is better? So I said: This one, and on his stand was a piece of silver. The people said: This is the sword of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq."
"25695","(25695) Issa ibn Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah, who said: I saw on a person wearing a lobed sword."
"25696","(25696) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: It was a local stolen sword."
"25697","(25697) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: Ali bin Al-Hussein came out to us The sword of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when I saw its cap and the two rings in which the straps were made, they were silver. He said: So I asked him, So when it was dissolved, it was the sword of Munabbih ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sahmi, which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took for himself. On the day of Badr, he said: And he brought out to us his armor, and behold, there was a delicate Yemeni woman with two giraffes. With its giraffes it is draped, and when it is sent it touches the earth. (Ibn Saad 486)"
"25698","(25698) Abu Nu`aym said, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: There is no harm in unhinging the sword."
"25699","(25699) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Māriq, on the authority of Tariq, who said: Ali addressed us, and upon him was a sword adorned with gold. Iron"
"25700","(25700) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ibn Habib Al-Muharbibi, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bayli. The companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Conquests have been won by peoples whose adornment was not gold, nor Silver, but its adornments were made of Alaabi, anodized, and iron. (Bukhari 2909 and Ibn Majah 2807)"
"25701","(25701) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Talha, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or pictures. (Bukhari 3322, Muslim 1665)"
"25702","(25702) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog, nor Pictures\n(Abu Dawud 2291, Ahmad 1/80)"
"25703","(25703) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, promised May God bless him and grant him peace. Gabriel quickly came to her, and he lamented on him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out and, lo, He saw Gabriel standing at the door and said to him: What prevented you from entering? He said: There is a dog in the house, and we do not enter a house in which there are pictures or a dog."
"25704","(25704) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Salami, Umm Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who said: Gabriel came to ask permission to come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave him permission. So he delayed it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his robe, and he stood up to him while he was at the door, and the Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: We have given you permission. He said: Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or pictures. (Tabarani 972)"
"25705","(25705) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bai, on the authority of Adiy, on the authority of Khalid bin Saad, who said: Abu Masoud was invited to a meal. He saw pictures in the house, so he did not enter until they were broken."
"25706","(25706) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Aslam, who said: When the age of the Levant came, a man from The chickens, and he said: I have prepared food for you, and I would like you to come, so that my people can see my honor upon you, and your status. With you, or as he said, and he said: We do not enter these churches, or he said: these shops, in which these Pictures"
"25707","(25707) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali; He hated pictures in homes."
"25708","(25708) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: Angels do not enter a house in which there are images. (Muslim 1472. Ahmad 2/305)"
"25709","(25709) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Asama bin Zaid bin Aslam told us, he said: My father told me; He built it on his brother, so Ibn Umar entered and saw pictures in the house, so he erased them, or scratched them, then he said: I heard the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog, or any pictures. (Bukhari 3227)"
"25710","(25710) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn ibn Waqid, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog."
"25711","(25711) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: He was on the shield of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, handed over a ram with a beautiful figure, so he divided that on him, and in the morning God had taken it away. (Ibn Saad 489)"
"25712","(25712) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Kuraib, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Asama, He said: I entered while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was feeling depressed, so I said: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of God? He said: Gabriel promised me that he would come to me, but he did not come to me for three days, then a dog passed by, and Asama said: So I placed my hand On my head and I woke up, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, started saying: What is the matter with you, O Asama? I said: A dog passed by, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered it to be killed, so it was killed, so Gabriel came to it and rushed to it, and said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Why did you delay, when you had not broken your promise when you promised me? He said: We do not enter a house in which there are dogs or pictures."
"25713","(25713) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not enter a house in which there were pictures, and that Ali would not enter a house in which there were pictures. Pictures"
"25714","(25714) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: Were they not the companions of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? Do they enter places in which there are pictures?"
"25715","(25715) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, who said: I entered with a stolen property lined up with statues, so he looked at me. A statue of it, and he said: What is this? They said: The statue of Mary."
"25716","(25716) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: There was in the house of Abraham an ark containing statues."
"25717","(25717) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a statue wearing a sword. There is no harm in it in the heavens of the House, but what is disliked among it is that which is placed in the accusative case, meaning pictures."
"25718","(25718) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, had been covered with a blanket containing statues. When he saw it, its color changed and he shook it with his hand. Then he said: Indeed, it is more severe. People will be punished on the Day of Resurrection because they resemble God’s creation. (Bukhari 6109. Muslim 91)"
"25719","(25719) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, the people who will be most severely tormented on the Day of Resurrection are those who make pictures. (Bukhari 5950, Muslim 98)"
"25720","(25720) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace be upon him: Photographers will be tortured on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Bring to life what you have created. (Bukhari 5951, Muslim 9786)"
"25721","(25721) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, who said: I entered Marwan’s house with Abu Hurairah. He saw pictures on it, and said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God says: And who is more unjust than he who goes? He creates a character like mine? So let them create grain, let them create offspring, and let them create barley. He said: Then he called for ablution and he performed ablution.\n(Bukhari 7559, Muslim 1671)"
"25722","(25722) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mihran, on the authority of Umair, a client of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of Usama, he said: I entered the Kaaba with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he saw pictures in the House, so he commanded me. So I brought him a bucket of water, and he started striking those pictures and saying: God will fight a people who make pictures of what they do not create. (Abu Dawud 623)"
"25723","(25723) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas bin Malik, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas. So he began to issue a fatwa, and he did not say, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said,” until a man asked him, and he said: “I am a man who draws pictures of this.” Pictures? Ibn Abbas said to him: Come closer to him, so the man approached, and Ibn Abbas said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Who He formed images in this world and was assigned to breathe the soul into them on the Day of Resurrection, and He is not a blower. (Bukhari 5963 and Muslim 1671)"
"25724","(25724) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Salama Abi Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah; In his saying: (Indeed, those who call upon Allah and His Messenger) he said: The owners of images."
"25725","(25725) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two sales and two clothes; As for the two trades: the touching, and the excommunication, and as for the two garments: the inclusion of the blind, and the concealment in one garment, it is not There is something about his relief (Abu Dawud 33700, Bukhari 2147)"
"25726","(25726) Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Khubayb ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hafs Bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wearing two types of clothing: covering a deaf woman, and hiding in one garment. Leading your relief to heaven. (Bukhari 584, Ibn Majah 3560)"
"25727","(25727) Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Saad bin Sa’id, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said, “No.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of two clothes; Including the deaf woman, and hiding in one garment while revealing your private parts.\n(Ibn Majah 3561)"
"25728","(25728) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah Abu Al-Munib Al-Ataki told us, he said: Tell us Abdullah bin Buraydah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace; He forbade two types of clothing and two sittings. As for the two types of clothing: you should pray in trousers and you do not have to wear anything else. A man prays in one garment and does not cover himself with it, and when sitting: he covers himself in one garment and his private parts are seen. He sits between the shade and the sun. (Abu Dawud 637)"
"25729","(25729) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Ja’far ibn Burqan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wearing two clothes. The fast one: which is when he is wrapped in one garment, raising his side above his shoulders, and he has no other garment on him, or A man covers himself with one garment, there is nothing between his private parts and the sky, meaning a covering. (Nasa’i 9748)"
"25730","(25730) Ibn Numayr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cursed the one who connects the line and the one who connects to it, and the one who does it and the one who does it. (Bukhari 5937, Muslim 119)"
"25731","(25731) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: Al-Qasim and Makhul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu In front of him; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the one who was connected and the one who was connected on the Day of Khaybar, the tattooed woman and the tattooed woman. And the rough one is her face, and the hard one is her pocket."
"25732","(25732) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma’, she said: A woman came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she said: My daughter is a groom, and she has been afflicted with measles, and her hair is splitting. Should I do her hair? What is it? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: May God curse the one who establishes it and the one who establishes it. (Bukhari 5936, Muslim 1676)"
"25733","(25733) Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God was cursed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the one who tattoos and the tattooed one, the one who connects him and the one who connects him. (Tirmidhi 1120, Ahmad 1/448)"
"25734","(25734) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Abu Asama, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the tattooer and the one who had the tattoo, the one who was connected to it and the one who was connected. (Ahmad 1/251)"
"25735","(25735) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ali; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the tattooed woman and the tattooed woman."
"25736","(25736) Hafs told us, on the authority of Razin, who said: I heard Fatima bint Ali bin Abi Talib say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was cursed. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. Continue poetry with poetry."
"25737","(25737) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, he said: I heard Al-Hasan bin Muslim It is narrated on the authority of Safiyya bint Shayba, on the authority of Aisha; A neighbor of the Ansar got married, and she fell ill and her hair became messy, so they wanted to pray for him, so they asked the Messenger of God May God bless him and grant him peace about that? So he cursed the one who continues it and the one who establishes it.\n(Muslim 1677. Ahmad 6/111)"
"25738","(25738) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Mu’awiyah presented Medina, so he addressed us and took out a cup of hair and said: I did not see anyone doing it except the Jews. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conveyed it, but he called it falsehood. (Bukhari 3488, Muslim 1680)"
"25739","(25739) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Ikrimah; He hated the impurity that women put in their heads."
"25740","(25740) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Falih narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abi"
"25741","(25741) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in disobedience if it is placed in different circumstances."
"25742","(25742) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Aqeel, on the authority of Bahiya, on the authority of Aisha; She forbade connecting hair."
"25743","(25743) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Thawr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no problem. With wesal if it is wool."
"25744","(25744) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr; On Ibn Omar’s journey, he saw a Qaysranian qatayfa."
"25745","(25745) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God was cursed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, or may God’s displeasure befall him, all of Ahimr’s journeys."
"25746","(25746) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Al-Ma’rur, on the authority of Hudhayfah; Omar saw a woman wearing red fences. He said: So he ordered me to cut her. He said: I said: It is wood. So he left her."
"25747","(25747) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Ibn Masoud borrowed an animal, and he brought it with a purple lining over it. He took it off and mounted it."
"25748","(25748) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Aaron, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Al-Ash'ari was brought to an animal with a purple linen over it, so he ordered it to be removed."
"25749","(25749) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, on the authority of a man from Banu Haritha, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him. And he handed over our mounts, and upon our camels were clothed with red eye threads, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. I see this red color has affected you? So we got up quickly, according to what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, until some of our camels ran off. He said: So we took the clothing. So We took it away from it. (Abu Dawud 4067. Ahmad 3/463)"
"25750","(25750) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubaira, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of the golden seal, and on the Mithra, meaning the red one. (Tirmidhi 2808 and Abu Dawud 4048)"
"25751","(25751) Ali bin Husayn narrated to us, saying: Al-Majishun Abd al-Aziz bin Abd Allah informed us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Utba. Ibn al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas said: I saw al-Sa’ib, Nimr’s sister’s son, riding with a red mithras."
"25752","(25752) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, saying: Ayyash ibn Abbas informed me. Al-Himyari, on the authority of Abu Al-Husayn Al-Hajri Al-Haytham, on the authority of Amir Al-Hajri, who said: I heard Abu Rayhani, the companion of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to forbid riding tigers."
"25753","(25753) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Mu’awiyah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade riding marmots and tigers.\n Ibn Sirin said: Muawiyah did not blame the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in hadith.\n(Abu Dawud 4126. Ibn Majah 3656)"
"25754","(25754) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: There is no harm in tiger skins if they are tanned."
"25755","(25755) Abdul narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham; That his father used to wear tiger saddles, or the skins of wild lions."
"25756","(25756) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: The skins of tigers were mentioned in the presence of Muhammad, and he said: It is only disliked to He would pray on it, and Muhammad saw no harm in riding on it, and he said: I do not know of anyone who left these skins. A sin."
"25757","(25757) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, who said: I asked Al-Hakam about tiger skins? He said: The skins of wild beasts are disliked."
"25758","(25758) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Omar wrote to the people of the Levant forbidding them to ride on the skins of lions."
"25759","(25759) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, A.S. Ibn Sirin; Ibn Masoud borrowed an animal, and it was brought to him wearing a pack of tigers. He took it off and mounted it."
"25760","(25760) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hakim ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ali ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger forbade May God bless him and grant him peace to cover the walls. (Bayhaqi 272)"
"25761","(25761) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar reported that his son He had his walls covered, so he said: By God, if that were the case, I would have burned his house."
"25762","(25762) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem ibn Abdullah, who said: I married during the time of my father, so my father called the people, and he was among those who gave Abu Ayyub’s call to prayer, and I covered my house with a green soldier. Then Abu Ayyub came and entered while my father was standing and looking. The house was covered by a green soldier. He said: O Abdullah, are you covering yourself? Walls? Then my father said, and was ashamed: The women defeated us, O Abu Ayyub. He said: Whoever fears that the women will defeat him, then I should not fear that They will overpower you, I will not feed you food, nor will I enter your house. Then they left. (Bayhaqi 272)"
"25763","(25763) Hafs told us, on the authority of Maymun Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim; He disliked women riding saddles."
"25764","(25764) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, who said: They used to hate a man riding a mirror, and riding A woman is for a man."
"25765","(25765) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They used to disdain men’s uniforms for women. Women's uniform for men."
"25766","(25766) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Umm Shabib, on the authority of Umm Omar; Al-Zubayr’s wife said: I heard Omar saying: O women, hide your henna, and remove the hijab, and I heard him saying: Sing. God is a woman who prays in detention."
"25767","(25767) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammam, who said: I asked, or I heard, or he was asked about the size of iron? He said: There is no problem with it."
"25768","(25768) Shababa told us, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, he said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari: Beware of this iron knee."
"25769","(25769) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Tu’amah al-Jaafari, who said: I saw Musa bin Talhah clenching his teeth with gold."
"25770","(25770) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qays, who said: I saw Nafi’ bin Jubayr with his teeth tied with steel. Gold"
"25771",""
"25772",""
"25773","(25773) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Hayyan, who said: Ibn Tarfi bin Arfaja narrated to me; That his grandfather’s nose was injured on the Day of Killing, so he took a nose made of paper and it stank on him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him. He was blessed to have a nose made of gold. (Abu Dawud 4229. Tirmidhi 1770)"
"25774","(25774) Zaid told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: I saw a Lebanese thābit with gold teeth clenched."
"25775","(25775) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Muhajir, he said: Ibn Umar said: Whoever wears a robe is evil. Or a garment of fame that God will clothe with fire on the Day of Resurrection. (Abu Dawud 4025. Ibn Majah 3607)"
"25776","(25776) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Husayn, he said: Zubaid Al-Yami was wearing a robe. He said: So I heard Ibrahim frowned upon him. He said: So I said to him: People used to wear them. He said: Yes, but whoever was has worn them out. He wears it, and if anyone wears it today, they will notice it and point to it with their fingers."
"25777","(25777) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Darda’, who said: Whoever rides a mounted animal, Or he wears a piece of clothing, may God turn away from it as long as it remains on him, even if He is generous to him."
"25778","(25778) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Muhajir Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever wears a shawl of The garment that God has clothed with His humiliation."
"25779","(25779) Shabab narrated to us, he said: Shu’ba narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Bukhari 5921, Ibn Majah 3638)"
"25780","(25780) Waki’ and Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hassan, who said: I heard my mother, Fatima bint Al-Hussein forbade Qaza’."
"25781","(25781) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: No. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about qaza’, and qaza’ means that a certain part of the boy’s head is shaved and another part is left.\n(Bukhari 5920, Muslim 1675)"
"25782","(25782) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Salam, who said: I entered upon Aisha and there was a fright in my head. So she ordered him to be cut off, or shaved."
"25783","(25783) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, I said: A man with a head like a bird’s head? He said: O son of my brother, we have not known of any of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to conclude that neither Abu Bakr, nor Omar, nor So-and-so, or so-and-so, until he counted some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I repeated bitterness against him, as if he hated it. The ring"
"25784","(25784) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, Tawoos, and Mujahid; Indeed, they did not seal anything."
"25785","(25785) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdullah bin A wise man, he said: The book of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has come to us: That you should not benefit from the dead by any honor or generosity.\n(Ibn Majah 3613 and Ahmad 4/310)"
"25786","(25786) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Ukaym said: The letter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us while we were in Jihan: Do not benefit from the dead. With love, and without fanaticism. (Tirmidhi 1729. Ibn Majah 3613)"
"25787","(25787) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdullah bin A wise man, who said: The letter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us while I was a boy: that you should not benefit from the honor of a dead person, nor of a descendant.\n(Abu Dawud 4124; Ibn Majah 3613)"
"25788","(25788) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu`bai, he said: I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about pig’s hair. Is it done? His thoughts"
"25789","(25789) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Jafar (h) and on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Indeed, they made it a concession to beaded with the hair of a pig."
"25790","(25790) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He did not wear sandals with beads made of pig's hair."
"25791","(25791) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Wasit, who said: I asked Abu Iyad about Pig hair, placed on the animal’s wound? His thoughts"
"25792","(25792) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, we conclude with this and this, meaning the index and middle fingers. (Muslim 64. Tirmidhi 1786)"
"25793","(25793) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Laith, who said: Abraham hated him."
"25794","(25794) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: I covered my side, meaning the inside, with pictures in it, so when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, he covered it. So I made two niches from it, and I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, leaning on one of them. (Muslim 92. Ibn Majah 3653)"
"25795","(25795) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d, a man from the people of Medina, who said: Ibn Sa’d narrated to me; Her father brought cushions from Persia that contained statues, so we used to spread them out."
"25796","(25796) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, who said: I saw Salem bin Abdullah leaning on a red pillow in it. Statues, so I said to him? He said: This is only disliked for the one who installs it and makes it."
"25797","(25797) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father; He used to lean on the places where there were statues. Birds and men."
"25798","(25798) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed on the authority of Hattan ibn Abdullah, he said: A friend of mine came to me and called me, so I looked over him and said: The letter of the Commander of the Faithful was read to us, intending to whomever he was. In his house there was a curtain erected with pictures of what he had placed. I was reluctant to stay the night as a sinner, so we got up to a place of ours. So I placed it. Muhammad said: They did not see what was stepped on and spread out of images like what was erected."
"25799","(25799) Ismail told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: It was said about pictures on pillows and rugs The one who has intercourse: This is humiliation for her."
"25800","(25800) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: They hated the statues that were erected as monuments. And they see no harm in what the feet have set upon."
"25801","(25801) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He saw no harm in the images he had intercourse with."
"25802","(25802) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated to depict a fruit tree."
"25803","(25803) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: There were statues of birds in the gathering of Muhammad. Some people were saying that, so Muhammad said: Indeed, these people have increased, so if only you had changed their meaning."
"25804","(25804) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Khalid, who said: There is no harm in pictures if they are Have intercourse"
"25805","(25805) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in pictures if She used to have intercourse."
"25806","(25806) Abd al-Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Regarding statues, if they are spread out, stepped on or spread out, there is no harm in it, and if they are erected, I hate them."
"25807","(25807) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He hated syllables, whether they were in the accusative or simple."
"25808","(25808) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The shape is only the head, so if it is cut, there is no problem."
"25809","(25809) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Salama Abi Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah; His saying: {Those who call out Allah and His Messenger} He said: The owners of images."
"25810","(25810) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I entered upon Al-Qasim while he was in the highest place of Mecca in his house, and I saw In his house there is a stone with pictures; The beaver and the phoenix."
"25811","(25811) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, he said: They did not see any harm in the images that were stepped on."
"25812","Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah told us:\n(25812) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hilal, on the authority of Jarir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who deprives kindness is deprived of goodness.\n(Muslim 2003. Abu Dawud 4776)"
"25813","(25813) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, who said: I asked Aisha, may God be pleased with her, about Bedouins, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to look at these hills, and he wanted to be a Bedouin once. So he sent to me a mahram she-camel of the al-Sadaqah camels, and said to me: O Aisha, be gentle, for gentleness has never been found in anything except He adulterated it, and nothing was ever removed from it except that it disgraced it. (Abu Dawud 2470, Ahmad 6/58)"
"25814","(25814) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Ali bin Mamluk, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever is given his share of kindness, will be given His share of goodness, and whoever is deprived of his share of kindness, will be deprived of his share of goodness. (Bukhari 444. Tirmidhi 2002)"
"25815","(25815) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hilal, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whoever deprives kindness also deprives goodness."
"25816","(25816) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hilal, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of the Prophet May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and grant him peace."
"25817","(25817) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: I have heard that it is written in the Torah, that gentleness is the root of Wisdom"
"25818","(25818) Waki’ told us, Ibn Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: It was said: Whoever is shown kindness in this world, it will benefit him in it. The Hereafter"
"25819","(25819) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, God A companion who loves gentleness, is generous, and helps with what does not help with violence."
"25820","(25820) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus and Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God is gentle and loves gentleness and pleases him, and gives what is not required of him. He gives violence. (Bukhari 672, Abu Dawud 4774)"
"25821","(25821) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of a man from Bali, who said: I entered with my father Ali. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from me, and I said to him: Oh father, what did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say to you? May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: He said to me: If you are concerned about the matter, then you must perform it, until God brings you a way out of your matter.\n(Bukhari 888)"
"25822","(25822) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, God Almighty A companion who loves gentleness, and gives in it what he does not give in the case of violence."
"25823","(25823) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Alaqah, who heard it from Usama bin Sharik, who said: A man said: O Messenger of God, what is the best thing that has been given to a servant? He said: good character."
"25824","(25824) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Mus’ar, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Alaqă, on the authority of Usama ibn Sharik, they said: Messenger of God, what is the best thing a Muslim has been given? He said: good character. (Tayalisi 1233. Tabarani 470)"
"25825","(25825) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Siyah Abi Yahya, on the authority of Imran bin Riyah, on the authority of Ali bin Amara, on the authority of Jabir bin Samarra, said: I was in a gathering in which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting, and Abu Samarra was sitting. In front of me, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indecency and indecency are not part of Islam in any way, and the best of people are Muslims. The best of them in character. (Tabarani 2072)"
"25826","(25826) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was not obscene or indecent, and he used to say: Among your best qualities are your virtues. Morally (Bukhari 3559. Muslim 1810)"
"25827","(25827) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The most perfect of people in faith, and the best of believers in faith are those with the best character, and the best of you are the best of you. For their women (Abu Dawud 4651. Ahmad 2/250)"
"25828","(25828) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He is the most perfect of believers in faith, the best in character, and the kindest to his family. (Tirmidhi 2412, Hakim 53)"
"25829","(25829) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah al-Khushaniya, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The most beloved of you to me and the closest to me on the Day of Resurrection is the one with the best morals. The furthest of you from me and the most hateful to me, the worst in morals, the talkative, the arrogant, the hypocritical. (Ahmad 4/1931 Ibn Hibban 482)"
"25830","(25830) Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The most complete of the believers in faith is the best of them. Creativity\n(Ahmad 2/527, Darmi 2792)"
"25831","(25831) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ma’bad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Harithah ibn Wahhab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Neither the one who passes away nor the one who passes away will enter the jinn, and the one who passes away is the harsh one.\n(Muslim 2190, Abu Dawud 4768)"
"25832","(25832) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, on the authority of Ata’ Al-Kikharani, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: There is nothing heavier on the scales than good character.\n(Abu Dawud 4766. Ahmad 6/446)"
"25833","(25833) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: O Mu’adh, and Waki’ said another time: O Abu Dharr, follow evil with good. wipe it out, and treat people with good manners."
"25834","(25834) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The worst of people on the Day of Resurrection is the one who fears his immorality. (Bukhari 6054, Abu Dawud 4758)"
"25835","(25835) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Mothers are morals. The Believer: indecency."
"25836","(25836) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hakim ibn Jabir, who said: A man said to another man: Advise me. He said: I will follow. A good deed erases it, and behave well towards people. (Tirmidhi 1987)"
"25837","(25837) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, who said: Zayd bin Thabit was one of the most intelligent people. When he is alone with his family, and his crisis is when he sits with the people."
"25838","(25838) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to her: O Aisha, do not be immoral. (Muslim 11. Ahmad 6/229)"
"25839","(25839) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Jadali, Abu Abdullah, he said: I said: To Aisha: What was the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: He was the best of people. He was not obscene, indecent, or loud in the markets. (Ahmad 6/236. Ibn Hibban 6443)"
"25840","(25840) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man from Jehanna, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The best thing a believer is given is good character, and the worst thing a man is given is a bad heart in beautiful images."
"25841","(25841) Zaid bin Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh narrated to us, on the authority of his father, Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father Shurayh, On the authority of his grandfather, Hani bin Yazid, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me something that will make me commit to the Jinn. He said: On you. By speaking well and by giving food.\n(Abu Dawud 4916. An-Nasa’i 5940)"
"25842","(25842) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sa’id, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: You will not please people with your money, so let them be satisfied with your goodness and good manners. (Bazzar 1977)"
"25843","(25843) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Omar said: According to the man: his religion and his chivalry: His character, and its origin: his mind."
"25844","(25844) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr informed me, on the authority of His father, he heard Al-Nawwas bin Samaan Al-Ansari say: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about righteousness and sin. He said: Righteousness is good character, and sin is what wavers within your soul and which you hate for people to find out about. (Bukhari 2950, Muslim 1980)"
"25845","(25845) Affan told us, he said: Abd al-Warith told us, he said: Abu al-Tayyah told us, he said: Anas told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the best of people in character. (Muslim 2671, Ahmad 3/212)"
"25846","(25846) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Khalaf bin Hawshab, on the authority of Maymun bin Mihran, who said: I said to Umm al-Darda’: What I heard from the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, something? She said: Yes, she entered upon him while he was sitting, or she said in the mosque, or she mentioned something else, so I heard him say: The first thing Good character is put in the scale. (Tabarani 647)"
"25847","(25847) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: It is written in the Torah: Your face will be beautiful and your speech will be kind. You will be more beloved to people than those to whom they give gifts."
"25848","(25848) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Faith has sixty-four chapters, or seventy-four chapters. The greatest of them is there is no god but Allah, and the lowest of us is removing harmful things from the path, and the living is a part of the faith (Bukhari 9. Muslim 58)"
"25849","(25849) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, that he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard He greeted a man who was advising his brother about modesty, and he said: Modesty is part of faith. (Muslim 591 Ahmad 2/9)"
"25850","(25850) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Living is a branch of faith. (Ibn Majah 57. An-Nasa’i 11737)"
"25851","(25851) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra mentioned, he said: Ashjaj bani Asr: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are two creatures in you that God loves. He said: I said: What are they? He said: Dreaming and modesty. He said: I said: Was it ancient or modern? He said: No, but long ago, I said: Praise be to God who created me with two creatures that God loves. (Nasa’i 7746. Ahmad 4/206)"
"25852","(25852) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Sawwar, on the authority of Imran bin Husain, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Life is all the best. (Bukhari 6117. Ahmad 4/426)"
"25853","(25853) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, God loves the living, the forbearing, the chaste, and hates the obscene, obscene, beggar, and the one who hides his covering."
"25854","(25854) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: modesty is a part of faith, faith is in the jinn, obscenity is a part of indecency, and indecency is in the Fire.\n(Tirmidhi 2009. Ahmad 2/501)"
"25855","(25855) His youth told us, he said: His people told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of a servant of Anas called Abdullah, he said: I heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was more shy than a virgin in her private room. He hated something that we knew about him. (Bukhari 3562. Ahmad 3/91)"
"25856","(25856) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, who said: His eyes entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not He asked for permission, and Aisha said: O Messenger of God, who is this? He said: This is an obedient fool among his people. He said: Then a drink was brought to him and he concealed himself. Then he drank and said: O Messenger of God, what is this? He said: This life is a trait among them. They have given it to you and you have withheld it."
"25857","(25857) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Abu Masoud, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The last thing that people understood of the words of the Prophet: If you are not ashamed, then do whatever you want. (Bukhari 3483. Ahmad 4/122)"
"25858","(25858) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A lack of modesty is blasphemy."
"25859","(25859) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Ya’la ibn Hakim, who said: My most suspicion is that it is on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr said: Ibn Omar said: Modesty and faith are linked together, so if one of them is removed, the other is removed. (Hakim 22)"
"25860","(25860) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Bakr, who said: Being shy is part of faith, and faith is in Paradise. And obscenity is part of the impurity, and the impurity is in the Fire."
"25861","(25861) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr (and Sayyid), who said: The Forbearing."
"25862","(25862) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Anas informed me, saying: Salma ibn Safwan informed me, on the authority of Zayd bin Talha bin Rukanani said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Everything has a character, and the character of faith Life (Ibn Majah 4181)"
"25863","(25863) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, among the living creatures there is a weakness. Indeed, there is reverence for God in him."
"25864","(25864) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Qaboos, a servant of Abdullah bin Amr, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, conveyed this message: The merciful will be merciful to the Most Merciful, be merciful to those on earth. May those in heaven have mercy on you. (Abu Dawud 4902. Tirmidhi 1924)"
"25865","(25865) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Jarir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: No, may God have mercy on those who do not have mercy on people. (Muslim 1809)"
"25866","(25866) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Jarir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: God does not have mercy on those who do not have mercy on people."
"25867","(25867) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted the like. (Bukhari 7376. Tirmidhi 1922)"
"25868","(25868) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Amir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr It was narrated that he said: Whoever does not have mercy on our youngest and knows the rights of our elders is not one of us. (Abu Dawud 4904. Ahmad 2/422)"
"25869","(25869) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Uthman, the client of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Harry, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the truthful and trustworthy Abul-Qasim, the owner of this stone: Do not remove it. Mercy, except for the wretched. His people said: I found it written with me. (Ahmad 2/301, Tayalisi 2529)"
"25870","(25870) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurayh, on the authority of his father, that a man, who said To the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I will slaughter a sheep and have mercy on it.” Or he said: “I will have mercy on a sheep when I slaughter it,” and he said: “I will have mercy on it.” If you have mercy on the sheep, may God have mercy on you twice. (Bukhari 373. Ahmad 3/436)"
"25871","(25871) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh bin Khalid Al-Sadusi, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of His brother, Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, said: God will have mercy on the sparrow."
"25872","(25872) Waki’ and Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Jarir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: God does not have mercy on those who do not have mercy on people."
"25873","(25873) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abd said: God: Have mercy on whoever is on earth, and whoever is in heaven will have mercy on you."
"25874","(25874) Abd al-Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: It has informed me that it is written in the Torah as You will have mercy, you will have mercy."
"25875","(25875) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: God only has mercy on His merciful servants."
"25876","(25876) Waki’ and Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: He who does not have mercy will not be shown mercy."
"25877","(25877) Ibn Uyayna told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: It is not permissible for a Muslim to shun his brother over three people. They will meet each other and he will repel one and the other will repel. The best of them is the one that begins with peace. (Muslim 1984. Tirmidhi 1932)"
"25878","(25878) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: It is not permissible for a Muslim to shun his brother for more than three days. (Bukhari 246. Abu Ali 716)"
"25879","(25879) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: No. He migrated among the Muslims for more than three years."
"25880","(25880) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Khaled bin Zaid, on the authority of Aamir bin Yahya Al-Maafiri, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: Whoever abstains from his brother for more than three days, he will be in Hell unless God protects him from it through his repentance."
"25881","(25881) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Do not envy one another, do not envy one another, do not turn to one another, and be servants of God as brothers, and do not let any of you abandon his brother for more than three days. Days.\n(Bukhari 60650 Muslim 1983)"
"25882","(25882) Ubaid bin Saeed Al-Qurashi told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, he said: I heard Sulaym bin Amir He narrates on the authority of Awsat bin Ismail bin Awsat that he heard Abu Bakr say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. Do not envy one another, do not hate each other, do not separate one another, do not turn to one another, and be servants of God as brothers.\n(Ibn Majah 3849. Talisi 5)"
"25883","(25883) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyy, on the authority of Anas, who said: There is no emigration among Muslims for more than three."
"25884","(25884) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Shabur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Some people were dragging a stone. He said: What is this? They said: The Hardest Stone. He said: Shall I not inform you of something worse than this? The one who is between him and his brother, and he overcomes Satan, so he comes to him and speaks to him. (Bazzar 2053)"
"25885","(25885) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, who said: Omar said: It is not permissible for a Muslim to desert his brother over his brother. Three days."
"25886","(25886) Khaled ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Hilal, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: It is not permissible for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days. (Muslim 1984, Abu Dawud 4878)"
"25887","(25887) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What do you consider epilepsy among you? He said: He is the one who is not struck by men. He said: No, but he is the one who controls himself when angry. (Muslim 2014, Abu Dawud 4746)"
"25888","(25888) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Make things easy and do not make things difficult.” He said it three times: “So if you get angry, keep quiet.” (Bazzar 152)"
"25889","(25889) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, on the authority of his cousin, Tamim, on the authority of Jariyah bin Qadamah, that he said: O Messenger of God, speak to me a word and say it less, so that I may become angry with you. He said: Do not get angry. So he repeated all of that to him repeatedly, saying: Do not be angry. (Ahmad 3/484)"
"25890","(25890) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf ibn Qais, on the authority of Jariyah ibn Qadamah, on the authority of A cousin of his from Banu Tamim, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the same. (Tabarani 2104)"
"25891","(25891) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Surad, who said: Two men sought refuge at The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made one of them’s eyes redden and his jugular veins swell, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: I know a word that if he had said this, the one who said: I seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan would have gone away from him and he said: Man: Do you think there is any madness in me? (Muslim 2015, Abu Dawud 47481)"
"25892","(25892) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Muadh, who said: Two men reproached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of them became very angry to the point of It seemed to me that his nose was tearing, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I would know a word if he said it. This is the wrath that has gone away: I seek refuge in God Almighty from the accursed Satan. (Abu Dawud 4747. Tirmidhi 3452)"
"25893","(25893) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Fear anger, for it is an embers kindled in the heart of the son of Adam. Have you not seen? The swelling of his veins and the redness of his eyes. Whoever feels any of that should stick to the ground. (Bukhari 2842. Muslim 121)"
"25894","(25894) Dawud bin Abdullah told us, he said: Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The severe person is not the one with epilepsy, but the strong person is the one who has power. His breath when angry. (Bukhari 6114 and Muslim 107)"
"25895","(25895) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: Advise me to speak, and do not speak harshly to me. He said: Avoid anger, so he returned to him, and he said: Avoid anger, so he returned to him and said: Avoid anger.\n(Ahmad 5/408, Malik 906)"
"25896","(25896) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf returned as a father Al-Raddad, and he said: The best of them and the best of them was Abu Muhammad, meaning Ibn Awf. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God said: I am God and I am the Most Merciful, and I am the Most Merciful. I have created a name for it from My Name. So whoever joins it, I will join you, and whoever breaks it. At this point (Tirmidhi 1907 and Abu Dawud 1691)"
"25897","(25897) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Abi Muzard, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The womb is attached to the throne. It says: Whoever joins me, may God bless him, and whoever cuts me off. God has cut it off. (Bukhari 5989. Muslim 1981)"
"25898","(25898) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: When the Messenger of By God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the people rushed towards him, so I came to him, and when I looked at him, I knew that his face was not In the face of a liar, the first thing I heard him say was: O people, spread the greetings, maintain the ties of kinship, and provide food. They prayed at night while the people were asleep. (Tirmidhi 2485. Ahmad 5/451)"
"25899","(25899) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: And the one who split The sea is for the Children of Israel. Indeed, in the Torah it is written: Son of Adam, fear your Lord, be righteous to your parents, and maintain your ties of kinship. I will extend to you Your life, and I will facilitate your ease, and avert from you your hardship."
"25900","(25900) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mughra’i, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He who fears his Lord and maintains ties with Him. He was blessed with mercy in his life, enriched his wealth, and was loved by his family. (Bukhari 5985)"
"25901","(25901) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Asim Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Qarib, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr says with a sharp tongue: Indeed, the womb is attached to the throne. She calls out with a sharp tongue: O God, bless whomever you have joined, and cut off whoever... He cut me off. (Tayalisi 2250)"
"25902","(25902) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: His leaders told us, on the authority of Abu Thumamah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The womb will be placed on the Day of Resurrection, and it will have a cage like ours. Spindle, speak with tongues freely and freely, so it joins whoever joins it, and cuts off whoever disconnects it. (Ahmad 2/189)"
"25903","(25903) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Jabbar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b al-Qurazi, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The womb is a protection from the Most Gracious. You will come on the Day of Resurrection. You say: O Lord, I have been cut off, O Lord, I have been wronged, O Lord, I have been wronged. (Bukhari 65. Ahmad 2/295)"
"25904",""
"25905",""
"25906",""
"25907","(25907) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: His father’s son does not repay him unless he finds it owned and buys it. Then he will free him."
"25908",""
"25909",""
"25910","(25910) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: To the mother is one-third of righteousness and to the father is one-third."
"25911","(25911) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Ali, on the authority of Abu Salami al-Salami, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I will bequeath a man three times to his mother, he will bequeath a man to his father, he will bequeath a man to his master who follows him, And if he is harmed by him, he will harm him. (Ahmad 4/311, Tabarani 4184)"
"25912","(25912) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ammarah ibn al-Qaqa’, and Ibn Shubramah, on the authority of Abu Zur’i, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, inform me of the people more deserving of good companionship than me. He said: Yes, and your father, you will prophesy, your mother, he said: Then who? He said: Your mother. He said: Then who? He said: Your father.\n(Muslim 1974 and Bukhari 5971)"
"25913","(25913) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ammar Abi Sa’id, he said: I said to Al-Hasan: To what extent do disobedience end? He said: To deprive them of them, to shun them, and to stare only at the face of your parents, O Amara, how righteous is this to them."
"25914","(25914) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asma’ Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Yunus Ibn Ubaid, who said: The one who is afflicted hopes for righteousness. Heaven, and the one who commits disobedience fears Hell."
"25915","(25915) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Righteousness Parents are sufficient for jihad. (Bukhari 3004, Muslim 1975)"
"25916","(25916) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Suleiman Al-Taymi informed us, on the authority of Saad bin Masoud, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: There is no Muslim who has parents and wakes up while doing good to them except that God opens for him two gates of Paradise, and he does not die in the evening. And he was on the wrong side of them, but God opened two gates of Hell for him, and neither of them was displeased with him, so God was satisfied with him even May God be pleased with him. He said: I said: Even if they were wrongdoers? He said: Even if they are wrongdoers."
"25917","(25917) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Salem bin Abi al-Ja’d, And Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Saeed, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No rebellious person, nor one addicted to alcohol, will enter Paradise. And there is no grace."
"25918","(25918) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: He was not righteous. His father is the one who pulled his gaze towards him."
"25919","(25919) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {So do not say to them, “Uff.” He said: When they reach old age. He was not afflicted with him when he was young, so do not say to them, “Fuck.”"
"25920","(25920) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha bin Muawiyah bin Jaimah. Al-Sulami, on the authority of his father, said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I want to wage jihad. With you for the sake of God. He said: He said: Is your mother alive? He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Hold your feet and then you will go to heaven. (Ibn Majah 2781, Hakim 151)"
"25921","(25921) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father {So do not say to him what is wrong} He said: No. You prevent them from doing something they wanted, or said: they liked."
"25922","(25922) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, who said: It was said to Muadh bin Jabal: The father’s right over the child? He said: If you had left your family and property, you would not have fulfilled your rights. His people said: Rather, Mansour bin Zazan narrated it to me, on the authority of The rule"
"25923","(25923) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Nubait bin Shurayt, on the authority of Jaban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: No disobedient person, nor an alcoholic, will enter Paradise. And there is no grace. (Nasa’i 5182. Ahmad 2/201)"
"25924","(25924) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: May God have mercy on a father who helped his son righteously."
"25925","(25925) Yazid bin Harun and Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Gabriel is still He advised me to be kind to my neighbor so much that I thought he would inherit from me. (Bukhari 6014 Muslim 2025)"
"25926","(25926) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Bashir bin Salman, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: We were sitting with Abdullah bin Amr and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, advising the neighbor to be kind to us, or we thought, that he He will inherit it. (Ahmad 2/160)"
"25927","(25927) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not harm his neighbor. (Bukhari 6018 and Muslim 68)"
"25928","(25928) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Salam bin Miskin informed us, saying: Shahr bin Hawshab narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Salam said that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My neighbor hurt me, so he said: Be patient. Then the second came to him and said: My neighbor hurt me, so he said: Be patient. Then the third came to him and said: My neighbor hurt me, so he said: Go to Throw your possessions into the plow, and if someone passes by you, say: My neighbor has hurt me, then the curse will be imposed on him, or it will become obligatory for him. Curse (Bukhari 125. Tabarani 356)"
"25929","(25929) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Dawud bin Faraij, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah narrating on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: Gabriel advised me to treat my neighbor so much that I thought he would be his heir. (Ibn Majah 3674. Ahmad 2/259)"
"25930","(25930) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, I seek refuge in You from an evil neighbor in the place of residence, for indeed the neighbor of the deserter He turns. (Bukhari 117, Ibn Hibban 1033)"
"25931","(25931) Yazid bin Harun told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Sinan Ibn Saad, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: He who does not believe is not a believer. His neighbors are his troubles. (Abu Ali 4236)"
"25932","(25932) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Abd ibn Abi Lubab, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: No one who harms his neighbor is small. (Tabarani 23)"
"25933","(25933) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, he said: He was a man of the Muslims. He was fasting, so he was making a piece for his suhoor meal, and the sheep came and took the piece, so the woman got up and unwrapped the sheep’s mouth. So she took the tablet, and the sheep bleed, and the man said: You would not know how much he bleated from your neighbour’s harm."
"25934","(25934) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, he said: The neighbor of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was throwing stones and carcasses at stones and said: O people of Quraysh, what kind of reward is this? (Ibn Saad 201)"
"25935","(25935) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Every good deed is done sincerely. (Ahmad 5/397)"
"25936","(25936) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Every good deed is done sincerely."
"25937","(25937) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The beginning of reason after faith in God is people’s understanding, and no man will perish after consulting him, and the people of goodness are in him. The people of this world are the people of good deeds in the hereafter. (Bayhaqi 109)"
"25938","(25938) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people of Those who do good in this world are the people of good in the hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the hereafter. The Hereafter"
"25939","(25939) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Whoever does good to rich and poor, So he told the truth."
"25940","(25940) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas narrated to us, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every good deed is done right. (Bukhari 231. Ahmad 4/307)"
"25941","(25941) Muhammad bin Hassan Al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Abdul Hamid Al-Basri narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every good deed is done truthfully (Bukhari 6021, Tirmidhi 1970)"
"25942","(25942) Malik told us, on the authority of Abu Awana, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Every good deed is done sincerely."
"25943","(25943) Yazeed bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Whoever supports three daughters will be sufficient for them and will have mercy on them and be kind to them. So he is in Paradise, or he said: With me in Paradise. (Ahmad 3/303, Abu Ali 2207)"
"25944","(25944) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever has a daughter to him and does not nurture her, does not insult her, and does not give preference to his son. Ali, meaning the males, may God admit him to Paradise. (Abu Dawud 5103, Hakim 177)"
"25945","(25945) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever has two daughters, or two sisters, treats them kindly as long as they are with him. He and I will be in Paradise like two girls - It means like the index finger and middle finger. (Muslim 2027. Tirmidhi 1914)"
"25946","(25946) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Shuhrabil bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever has two daughters and treats them well as long as they are friends with him, or with them, God will admit him to Paradise. With what\n(Ibn Majah 3470. Ahmad 1/235)"
"25947","(25947) Dawud bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Abdulaziz bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih Al-Samman, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman bin Mukmal, on the authority of Ayoub bin Bashir Al-Muawwi, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: None of you has three daughters or three sisters and does good to them unless he enters into Heaven"
"25948","(25948) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever supports two female slaves until they reach puberty will come on the Day of Resurrection. I And so he joined his fingers. (Muslim 2027. Tirmidhi 1914)"
"25949","(25949) Musab bin Al-Miqdam told us, he said: Mandal told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Omar bin Nabhan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who has three daughters and is patient with them. We have admitted you to Paradise by virtue of the mercy of them. A man said: And two? He said: And two. A man said: And one? He said: And one. (Ahmad 2/335 Hakim 176)"
"25950","(25950) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: He passed by me. Amr ibn Bulil: I was in the morning in the palm trees, and he moved me with his foot and said: Shall I lie down during the hour in which servants are spread out? God"
"25951","(25951) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Zubair used to forbid his sons from In the morning, he said: And Urwah said: I hear a man praying in the morning, so I pray to him."
"25952","(25952) Hafs told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Farukh, on the authority of Talha ibn Ubaid Allah, that He passed by a son of his who had woken up in the morning, and he mentioned that he had stopped him, and he forbade him from doing so."
"25953","(25953) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, who said: Ibn Al-Zubayr and Ubaid bin Umair met. Then they remembered something, and the other said to him: Did you not know that the earth is roaring to its Lord from the sleep of its scholars?"
"25954","(25954) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Zubair said: I will add more to the man. In the morning"
"25955","(25955) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, he said: He was safe and did not wake up in the morning, and he It is said"
"25956","(25956) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, similar to him."
"25957","(25957) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhul like him."
"25958","(25958) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, that she was Good morning"
"25959","(25959) Shababā told us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Shammās, he said: I came to Umm Salamah I found her sleeping - meaning after the morning."
"25960","(25960) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, that when the sun rose, Aisha fell asleep. His mid-morning sleep."
"25961","(25961) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, who said: I came to Sa`id ibn Jubayr and found him sleeping soundly. The sacrifice"
"25962","(25962) He said: He said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to wake up in the morning."
"25963","(25963) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Madini, who said: Omar came on the morning of Sahib and found him dead. He woke up in the morning, then he sat until he woke up, then Suhayb said: The Commander of the Faithful is sitting in his seat, and Suhaib is soft and morning. Then Omar said to him: I did not like you to let sleep accompany you."
"25964","(25964) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Zubair was harsh with women, and he was He breaks the sticks of mourning over them."
"25965","(25965) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Omar used to beat women and servants."
"25966","(25966) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: No. You shall strike your servant, and you shall strike your wife and your children."
"25967","(25967) Abdă narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that men were forbidden from hitting women, and it was said: They will not He strikes your best ones. Al-Qasim said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the best of them. He did not strike you.\n(Abu Dawud 2139. Bayhaqi 304)"
"25968","(25968) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not strike May God bless him and grant him peace, neither his servant nor his woman, nor does he strike anything with his hand. (Muslim 1814, Abu Dawud 4753)"
"25969","(25969) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Kathir, on the authority of Asim bin Laqit bin Sabria, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not strike your female slave the way your female slave strikes you."
"25970","(25970) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, he said: He said: Ammar: Whoever strikes his servant unjustly will be punished by him."
"25971","(25971) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zam’i, he said: The Prophet gave a speech May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then he mentioned the women, and he admonished them about them and said: Why should one of you flog his wife like the flogging of a slave woman? Perhaps To have sex with her at the end of his day. (Bukhari 4942. Muslim 2191)"
"25972","(25972) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Hanzala, on the authority of Ammar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever has two faces in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection. (Abu Dawud 4840, Darami 2764)"
"25973","(25973) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that a man greeted the Prophet three times, but he did not respond. Then it was said to him: Why? He said: He has two faces."
"25974","(25974) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: You will find among the worst people in the sight of God on the Day of Resurrection the one with two faces. (Bukhari 6058. Tirmidhi 2025)"
"25975","(25975) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Luqman Dhu Two-faced people are not trustworthy with God. (Bukhari 313. Ahmad 2/365)"
"25976","(25976) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Malik ibn Asma’ ibn Kharijiya, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Ibn Masoud says: Indeed, he who has two tongues will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection. (Tabarani 9168)"
"25977","(25977) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Ibrahim saw me while I was blowing my nose, so he rebuked me and said: You should use your left hand, and do not get used to stepping with your right hand."
"25978","(25978) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was The right side of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was for his food and prayer, and his left was for everything else. (Bukhari 1688, Muslim 66)"
"25979","(25979) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of a traveler, on the authority of Ruzaiq ibn Siwar, that Al-Hasan ibn Ali smeared his right hand."
"25980","(25980) Abdă bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of the Amish, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated that a man should transgress his sexual intercourse. With his right hand"
"25981","(25981) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam Abu Muadh, who said: I saw Al-Hasan blowing his right hand."
"25982","(25982) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man has more right to the chest of his animal."
"25983","(25983) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Rafi’, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Abu Sa’id He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man has more right to the chest of his animal, and if he returns to his place, he has more right to it.\n(Muslim 1715. Abu Dawud 4819)"
"25984","(25984) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It used to be said: A man has more right to the chest of his animal. And his bed."
"25985","(25985) Muhammad bin Al-Fadhil narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Attar, who said: I saw Al-Sha’abi standing behind a man. He said: And he was He says: The owner of the animal has more right to its priority."
"25986","(25986) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Issa bin Asim, who said: Abdullah said, The man has more right to a chest. His animal: And the man has more right to the top of his bed."
"25987","(25987) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Habib bin Shahid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, that Muadh bin Jabal The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brought an animal for him to ride, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: Lord of the animal. Is he more worthy of her breast? He said: Then Muadh said: Here it is for you, O Prophet of God. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode, and Muadh followed.\n(Tirmidhi 2773 and Abu Dawud 2565)"
"25988","(25988) Shababah told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: I saw Hamid bin Hilal and Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, Ata and Bakr bin Abdullah do not trim their moustache."
"25989","(25989) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hilal, who said: I saw Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and Omar bin Abdul Aziz. And safe and sound, Urwa bin Al-Zubair, Ja’far bin Al-Zubair, Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, and Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman. Ibn Al-Harith Ibn Hisham do not trim their moustache very much, they take a good part of it."
"25990","(25990) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qays, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, and Aarak bin Malik: the same."
"25991","(25991) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’iya, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of Simak ibn Zayd, he said: It was Ali takes some of his beard from what is next to his face."
"25992","(25992) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Ayyub from the descendants of Jarir, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, he said: It was Abu Hurairah grabs his beard, then takes what is left over."
"25993","(25993) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, he said: They liked to They keep their beards clean, except during Hajj or Umrah, and Abraham used to trim the part of his beard."
"25994","(25994) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he was taken from His beard, and it is not obligatory for him."
"25995","(25995) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They used to make concessions on what was in excess of the amount taken. The beard should be taken from it."
"25996","(25996) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: Whenever Al-Qasim shaved his head, he would take some of his beard. And drink it."
"25997","(25997) Ali bin Hashim and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that it was He takes what is above the fist, and Waki’ said: It is not permissible to take the fist."
"25998","(25998) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his followers, he said: Jabir said: We do not take from its length except during Hajj, or Omar"
"25999","(25999) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Zur`a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He used to take from his beard what was permissible to seize."
"26000","(26000) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, who said: I asked Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin and they said: There is no harm in taking it for a long time. Your beard"
"26001","(26001) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to cover their meat and take From its symptoms"
"26002","(26002) Wakī` narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mughirā, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked to omit every word or as a kurd. Yarkush"
"26003","(26003) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Groom the mustaches and grow the beard. (Bukhari 5893. Muslim 222)"
"26004","(24004) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Suhayb, on the authority of Habib bin Yasar, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who does not take something from his drinker is not one of us. (Tirmidhi 2761)"
"26005","(26005) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Othman Al-Haatibi, who said: I saw Ibn Omar trimming his moustache."
"26006","(24006) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Habib, who said: I saw Ibn Umar trimming his moustache. As if he had shaved it."
"26007","(26007) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan and Muhammad that they kept their moustaches."
"26008","(26008) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: I saw Abdullah trimming his moustache."
"26009","(26009) Qubaisa bin Uqba narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’, he said: I saw Abu Sa’id, Rafi’ bin Khadij, Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, Ibn Umar, Jabir bin Abdullah, and Abu Asayd. They make their mustaches the brother of the throat."
"26010","(26010) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Huraim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: We were commanded to give good news to the mustaches."
"26011","(26011) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Omar, who said: Omar bin Abd al-Aziz was asked: What is the Sunnah in narration? The mustache? He said: It is cut until the frame appears, and the excess of the drinkers is cut off."
"26012","(26012) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’qil, on the authority of Maymun, who said: Ibn Umar used to cut off his mustache and reward him as He shears the sheep."
"26013","(26013) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Abu Al-Umays told us, on the authority of Abdul Majeed bin Suhail, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Allah ibn Utbah said: A man from the Magians came to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. He had shaved his beard and grown his mustache long, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: What is this? He said: This is in our religion. He said: In our religion, we trim the mustache and grow the beard. (Muslim 222. Ahmad 2/366)"
"26014","(26014) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He took The one who drinks from religion. (Tirmidhi 2760, Ahmad 1/301)"
"26015","(26015) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, would trim his mustache, and Abraham, the friend of God, would trim his mustache, or some of his mustache."
"26016","(26016) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We were commanded to pay the debts. The strands of hair, and we take from the mustaches. (Abu Dawud 4198. Ahmad 5/265)"
"26017","(26017) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Mus`ab ibn Shaybi, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is part of the common sense to trim the mustache and grow the beard.\n(Bukhari 6287 and Muslim 1663)"
"26018","(26018) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his uncle, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, lying down in the mosque, with one of his legs placed on the other."
"26019","(26019) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Malik, on the authority of Ubayyah, he said: He entered upon Omar or was seen lying down with one leg crossed over the other."
"26020","(24020) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, that he saw Usama bin Zaid sitting with one leg crossed over the other."
"26021","(24021) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to lie down and put one of his legs on it. The Hereafter"
"26022","(24022) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Usama, on the authority of Nafi’: Ibn Umar said: He lies on his back and places one He does not see any harm in that, and he does it while sitting, and he does not see any harm in that."
"26023","(26023) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Only the people of The book, and Amer and Muhammad bin Ali said: There is no harm in it."
"26024","(26024) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn al-Ghasil, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to me that Bilal did: put one His legs are on top of each other."
"26025","(24025) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz al-Majishun, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, that Omar and Uthman They were doing it. (Bukhari 475, Abu Dawud 4834)"
"26026","(24026) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his uncle, he said: I saw Ibn Masoud was in the woods, lying down, placing one of his legs on top of the other, and he was saying: “Our Lord, do not make us a test for the people.” The wrongdoers}"
"26027","(24027) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran - meaning Ibn Muslim - who said: I saw a man placing one of his His legs are on top of each other."
"26028","(26028) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I asked Abu Majliz about a man who sits. And he placed one of his legs on top of the other and said: There is no harm in him, but it is something that the Jews hated. They said: He is a created being. The heavens and the earth in six days, then He established Himself on the Sabbath and sat for that session."
"26029","(24029) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Harun ibn Ri'ab said to him while he was sitting: On his bed, placing one of his legs over the other: Is this disliked, O Abu Bakr? He said: No."
"26030","(24030) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ bin Al-Mundhir told me, he said: My father told me, he said: I saw Muhammad bin The Hanafi one, placing one leg on the other."
"26031","(26031) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Israel, he said: He was told: Did you see Al-Sha’abi putting one of the His legs are on top of the other? He said: Yes."
"26032","(26032) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Ismail Rashid, who said: I lay down and rose up. One of my feet was on my knees, so Saeed gave me pebbles, then he said: Ibn Abbas used to forbid this."
"26033","(26033) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he disliked to lie down. He places one of his legs on top of the other."
"26034","(26034) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Wasil, that Jarir sat and placed one of his legs on the other and said: He has a heel: put it down, for this is not suitable for humans."
"26035","(26035) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Murā, on the authority of Amr ibn Utbah ibn Farqad, that Ka’b, He said to him: Put it down, for this is not suitable for human beings."
"26036","(26036) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, who said: Muhammad saw me with my feet placed like this and he placed his right foot. On his left thigh. He said: So he said: Raise it. They had colluded to hate her. He said: So it was mentioned to Al-Hasan. He said: The Jews hated it, but the Muslims disagreed with them."
"26037","(26037) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked for a man to sit and lie down. He turned his back on his thigh and said: It is Al-Tawrak."
"26038","(26038) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he forbade it."
"26039","(26039) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, that he disliked sitting as a ruler and said: “His sitting is a kingdom.”"
"26040","(26040) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, he said: Aamir informed me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Abbas said to his son Abdullah bin Abbas: O my son, I see the Commander of the Faithful approaching you and consulting you with some of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s peace and blessings be upon him, and he will be alone with you, so keep three things from him: Fear God. He will not tell you a lie, and do not reveal a secret from him. And do not backbite anyone in his presence. He said: So I said to Ibn Abbas: O Abu Abbas, each one of them is better than a thousand. He said: And who Ten thousand"
"26041","(26041) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Murra, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shihab, he said: Omar said: Do not object to what does not concern you, stay away from your enemy, and keep from your friend except the trustworthy, for the trustworthy is not equal to anything. Do not accompany The ungodly, and he will teach you of his immorality, and do not reveal your secret to him, and consult those who fear God regarding your matter."
"26042","(26042) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: Do not narrate a hadith to someone who does not know it, for whoever does not He knows that it harms him, but does not benefit him."
"26043","(26043) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Humaid al-Tawil told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: I was with the young men and he passed by us. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, greeted us, then he sent me on Hajj and sat against a wall or in the shade until I came to him. So I fulfilled his need, and when I came to Umm Sulaim, she said: What kept you imprisoned today? I said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent on a pilgrimage. She said: What is it? I said: It is a secret. She said: So keep the secret of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I have never told anyone about it. (Bukhari 1139. Muslim 145)"
"26044","(26044) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Hubaira Yahya bin Abbad, who said: The Muslim is a mirror. His brother, so if he takes something from him, let him show it to him."
"26045","(26045) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ghalib, who said: I asked Al-Hasan or a man asked him about the man, and he took something from the man. So He says: Let no evil happen to you, or evil is turned away from you. He said: So He says: He says: Let no evil happen to you, for it will only happen to you. Better than having it and then leaving it."
"26046","(26046) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, who said: Umar said: If one of you takes something from his brother... Something, let him show it to him."
"26047","(26047) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ubaid Allah al-Taymi, who said: I heard my father say: I heard Abu Hurairah says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One of you is the mirror of his brother, so if he sees harm Let him protect him from it.\n(Bukhari 239. Abu Dawud 4882)"
"26048","(26048) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Husayn, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: He was among Khalid. Ibn Al-Walid and Saad had a conversation, he said: Then a man had a meal with Khaled at Saad’s, he said: And he said: Saad: Meh, for what is between us has not... He reaches our religion."
"26049","(26049) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Zayd ibn Suhan, who said: Omar said: What will prevent you then? Have you seen a man who violates people's honor, so that you do not attack him? They said: Let us be careful of his tongue. He said: That is the most important thing for you to be witnesses."
"26050","(26050) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais, that Amr bin Al-Aas passed by a dead mule and said: To his companions: If one of you eats of this until he fills his stomach, it is better than eating the flesh of his Muslim brother."
"26051","(26051) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Al-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said to him: What is the unseen, O Messenger of God? He said: He mentioned your brother in a way that he disliked. He said: What do you think if there is something wrong with my brother, what should I say, O Messenger of God? He said: If your brother has what you say, then you have backbited him, and if there is not what you say, then you have slandered him. (Muslim 2001, Abu Dawud 4841)"
"26052","(26052) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Darda’, that a man had intercourse with another man. Another responded, and Abu Al-Darda' said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whoever protects his brother's honor is a sinner. He has a veil from the Fire. (Tirmidhi 1931. Ahmad 6/450)"
